hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"26053","(26053) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Aoun, who said: A man fell in love with another man, and another attacked him, and Umm al-Darda’ said: He did. I am proud of you. Indeed, whoever defends his brother’s honor, may God protect him. Mas’ar said: he blew, or the breath of fire."
"26054","(26054) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: If you say what is in the man, then you do not pay zakat on him."
"26055","(26055) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Alaqah, on the authority of Usama ibn Sharik, who said: I witnessed the Bedouins asking The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Is there a burden on us in such-and-such? He said: Servants of God, God has removed the hardship, except for whoever borrows something from his brother’s honor, that is the one who is embarrassed."
"26056","(26056) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, who said: If you saw a cut, then you remembered it and said Al-Aqta' was unseen. He said: So I mentioned it to Abu Ishaq, and he said: He spoke the truth."
"26057","(26057) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Bakr, on the authority of his father, Abu Musa al-Ash’ari said: If I saw a man suckling a sheep on the road and made fun of him, I would fear that I would not die until I suckled it."
"26058","(26058) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Hassan informed us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: If you say what is in it, and he does not listen, then you have backbited him, and if you say what is not in it, then you have slandered him."
"26059","(26059) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: If I had mocked a dog, I would have feared that I am a dog."
"26060","(26060) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Calamity is assigned by word."
"26061","(26061) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If you say what is in it, Then you have backbited him, and if you say something that is not in it, then you have slandered him."
"26062","(26062) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: I was holding Abraham’s hand while we wanted to The mosque. He said: I mentioned a man and backbited him. He said, so Abraham said to me: Go back and perform ablution. They used to consider this a form of slander."
"26063","(26063) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, that he had a comb made of elephant bones. And a city of elephant bones."
"26064","(26064) Abdă told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw my father in a city of elephant bones."
"26065","(26065) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that he had an ivory tile that he used to paint in."
"26066","(26066) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Suriya by Omar bin Abdul Aziz, she said: You brought him an ivory comb, or an ivory comb. He thought about it and said: He is dead."
"26067","(26067) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he hated ivory."
"26068","(26068) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he hated ivory."
"26069","(26069) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he hated all ivory, and that it be taken from it. comb"
"26070","(26070) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khuzaymah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade Dismounting is nothing but stupidity. (Abu Dawud 4156. Tirmidhi 1756)"
"26071","(26071) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Juwayriyah ibn Asma’, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar might have condemned Twice today."
"26072","(26072) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, except for stupidity."
"26073","(26073) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Shaibah bin Hisham, on the authority of Mughirah bin Al-Harith, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Dismounting is foolishness."
"26074","(26074) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They used to hate stepping out every day."
"26075","(26075) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If there are three, then two should not go to each other without the other. Ibn Numayr said: They should talk to one another. (Muslim 1717. Ahmad 2/141)"
"26076","(26076) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: If we are three, two people should talk to each other without one, that would make him sad until he mixes with people.\n(Muslim 1718 and Bukhari 6290)"
"26077","(26077) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: If there are three people, then Two are produced without one, for that is worse."
"26078","(26078) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, he said: I saw Ibn Omar He was conversing with a man, so I put my head between them, and Ibn Umar hit my chest and said: If you see two people conversing, do not You shall not enter between them except with their permission."
"26079","(26079) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If the people are four, then no. It is unfortunate for two people to communicate without each other. (Abu Dawud 4818)"
"26080","(26080) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who heard Jabir say: A man passed through the mosque with arrows, and he said to him: The Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Hold on to her blades."
"26081","(26081) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Buraid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of his father, who said: If one of you passes by The mosque with arrows, let him hold its blades."
"26082","(26082) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw A people were dealing with a sharp sword, and he said: May God curse those. So I said to Al-Hasan: He was in the mosque, and he said: No, but in it. As spacious as the mosque. (Ahmad 5/41. Hakim 290)"
"26083","(26083) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Cursed is he who gives his brother the sword drawn in his mouth. The mosque"
"26084","(26084) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Aslam al-Manqīrī, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, He hated drawing the sword in the mosque."
"26085","(26085) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever gives his brother the sword, let him sheath it."
"26086","(26086) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, lest he handle the drawn sword. (Tirmidhi 2163 and Abu Dawud 2581)"
"26087","(26087) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He asked for permission to handle a drawn sword, and he passed by a people handling a drawn sword and said: Did I not forbid you from this? May God curse whoever did this. (Ahmad 3/361)"
"26088","(26088) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd Ibn Jad’an, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: A man does not stand up for another man, but rather to enlarge him."
"26089","(26089) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace And he greeted him. He said: None of you should lead his brother to sit in it and then sit in it. He said: And when Ibn Umar used to stand up for him, He did not sit in it. (Muslim 1714. Ahmad 2/89)"
"26090","(26090) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: A man should not raise another man from his seat and then sit in it, but spread out and expand.\n(Muslim 1714. Ahmad 2/16)"
"26091","(26091) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbah bin Sa’id, on the authority of a servant of Abu Musa, On the authority of Sa`id bin Abi al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that he was called to bear witness, and a man from his gathering stood up and said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade, when a man stood up, another man from sitting in it, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a man should wipe his hand with the garment of someone who does not cover it. (Abu Dawud 4794. Ahmad 5/44)"
"26092","(26092) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Falayh narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abi Yaqub, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man should not stand up for another man when he sits. But make room, and God will make room for you. (Ahmad 2/338)"
"26093","(26093) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: It was disliked for a man to get up from... Its a place for the man to sit in."
"26094","(26094) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Adbas, on the authority of Abu Marzuq, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us, leaning on a staff, so we stood up to him and said: Do not stand as foreigners stand, venerating one another. (Abu Dawud 5187, Ibn Majah 3836)"
"26095","(26095) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Shahid, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Mu’awiyah entered a house in which... Abdullah bin Amir, and Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, so Abdullah bin Amer stood up, but Abdullah bin Al-Zubair did not, so Mu’awiyah said To Ibn Amir: Sit down, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Who is pleased with men imitating themselves in standing for him? Let him take his seat in the Fire. (Tirmidhi 2755, Abu Dawud 5186)"
"26096","(26096) Affan, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: There was no person more beloved to them than the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when they saw him they would not get up because of what they knew of his hatred for that.\n(Tirmidhi 2754)"
"26097","(26097) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tariq, who said: We were sitting with Al-Sha’abi, when Jarir bin Zayd, so Al-Sha’bi called for a pillow for him, and we said to him: O Abu Amr, we have old people with you. I prayed for this boy. With a pillow? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a noble person comes to you, be generous to him."
"26098","(26098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If A noble man has come to you, so honor him. (Abu Dawud 511)"
"26099","(26099) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Asim, he said: Abu Qalaab presented it to a gentleman and said: Abu Qalaba: It used to be said: Do not deny your brother his honor."
"26100","(26100) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali and a man entered, and he laid out for them two pillows. So Ali sat down and the other did not sit down, so Ali said: No one can return the karama except a donkey."
"26101","(26101) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Take the wisdom from whomever you have heard. It is just like an archer from someone other than the archer."
"26102","(26102) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya bin Abi Zaydi narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Al-Aqmar narrated to me, that Abu Juhayfah used to say: Sit with the great ones, mix with the wise men, and ask the scholars."
"26103","(26103) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khattimi, that his grandfather Umair bin Habib advised his sons and said: O my sons, beware of sitting with the fools, for sitting with them is a disease. Indeed, he who dreams about the fool is pleased with his dream, and he who loves it regrets it, and he who does not acknowledge the little that he brings with it. The foolish person admits to many things, and if one of you wants to enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, let him settle himself. He must be patient in the face of harm, for he who is patient will never find harm to touch him."
"26104","(26104) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: Part of the jurisprudence of a man is his walking. And his introduction, Abu Qalabab said: May God kill the poet when he says:\nOn the authority of the man: Do not ask and see his companion, and every companion is guided by comparison."
"26105","(26105) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Murā or Ḥubayra, who said: Abdullah said: Consider the people. By deceiving them"
"26106","(26106) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Maymun Al-Janni Abi Mansour, who said: I heard Ibrahim say: When he entered One of you has a house, and wherever they sit in it, let him sit, for they know best the nakedness of their house."
"26107","(26107) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, who said: I saw a man walking briefly."
"26108","(26108) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: It is disliked to be short. In prayer, because Iblis was brought down briefly."
"26109","(26109) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Atiyya, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: If a man speaks to another With a hadith and he said: Remain silent about me, for it is a trust."
"26110","(26110) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, the same."
"26111","(26111) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ata, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Jabir bin Atik, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If a man speaks to another man With the hadith, then he turned around and it was safe. (Abu Dawud 4835. Tirmidhi 1959)"
"26112","(26112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Beware of lying, for lying leads to immorality, and immorality leads to the Fire, and indeed the man To lie and try to lie until he is written before God as a liar, and against you[corrupt] With honesty, for honesty is righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise, and a man is truthful and strives for honesty until it is recorded with God. Friend. (Muslim 1050, Abu Dawud 4950)"
"26113","(26113) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā ibn Sharāhil, who said: Abdullah said: The man He will tell the truth and strive for truthfulness until there is no place for a needle in his heart for immorality to remain, and indeed he will not lie. He tries to lie until the truth has the place of a needle to settle in his heart."
"26114","(26114) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Mu’mar, on the authority of Abdul God, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It is not appropriate to lie in seriousness or in jest. Then Abdullah recited {Fear Allah and be with the truthful}"
"26115","(26115) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abu Bakr said: Beware of lying, for it is wrong. Faith"
"26116","(26116) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The believer is covered with all good deeds other than betrayal and lying."
"26117","(26117) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, He said: All good qualities are imprinted on the believer, except for betrayal and lying. (Bazzar 1139. Abu Ali 707)"
"26118","(26118) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, saying: It was mentioned by Amir that the hypocrite who If he told a lie, Amer said: I don’t know what you are saying? If he is a liar, then he is a hypocrite."
"26119","(26119) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Umar, who said: Do not convey the message. The truth of faith is until you abandon lying in jest."
"26120","(26120) Zaid told us, he said: Aoun told us, he said: Lying was mentioned to Muhammad in war, that there is nothing wrong with it, Muhammad said: I do not know how to lie unless it is forbidden."
"26121","(26121) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: It was narrated to us on the authority of Abu Imamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: The believer commits all good deeds other than betrayal and lying. (Ahmad 5/252)"
"26122","(26122) Shababih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, that a man from the loyalists of Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi’ Al-Adawi, He told him on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir, that he said: My mother called me one day while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting there. Our house, and she said: Come, I will give it to you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: And what did you want to give him? She said: Dates, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: If you had not given him anything, it would have been written down for you. A lie\n(Abu Dawud 4952. Ahmad 3/447)"
"26123","(26123) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Four things are: Whoever is in them is a pure hypocrite, and whoever is in them is a pure hypocrite. There was a trait of hypocrisy in him until he abandoned her: when he spoke he lied, when he promised he broke it, and when he promised he betrayed. And when he quarrels, he becomes ungrateful. (Muslim 1060; Abu Dawud 4455)"
"26124","(26124) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Abdullah said: Consider The hypocrite has three things: when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, and when he makes a promise he betrays. (Nasa’i 11754)"
"26125","(26125) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Subih bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: There are three things whoever is in it is a hypocrite: when he speaks, he lies, when he breaks a promise, and when he is trusted, he betrays: He said: And he recited these verses: {And among them are those who covenanted with Allah if He gave us of His bounty} to his saying: {hypocrisy in their hearts} to his saying: {because they were They lie.} (At-Tawbah: 75 at 77)"
"26126","(26126) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are three things whoever is in it is a hypocrite: he who tells a lie, breaks a promise when he is trusted, and betrays a trust when he is trusted.\n(Bukhār 331, Tirmidhi 2631)"
"26127","(26127) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Three who are among them, then he is a hypocrite, even if he fasts He prayed and said, “I am a Muslim.” When he spoke, he lied, when he was trusted, he betrayed, and when he made a promise, he broke it."
"26128","(26128) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever narrates a hadith on his authority while he sees it, it is a lie. He is one of the liars.\n(Tirmidhi 2462. Ahmad 4/252)"
"26129","(26129) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever narrates a hadith from him while he sees that it is a lie, then he is one. Liars\n(Ibn Majah 39. Ahmad 20)"
"26130","(26130) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar hadith of Samurah. (Ibn Majah 38)"
"26131","(26131) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Khubayb told me, on the authority of Hafs bin Asim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: It is enough of a lie for a man to narrate everything he hears. (Muslim 5. Abu Dawud 4953)"
"26132","(26132) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar said: It is enough for a person to tell lies. To narrate everything he heard."
"26133","(26133) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: According to It is a liar for a person to narrate everything he heard."
"26134","(26134) Harami bin Amara bin Abi Hafsa told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of a man, who said: Shurayh said: A dream is a treasure. Provided."
"26135","(26135) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, who said: Al-Sha’bi said: Knowledge is adorned. A dream of his family."
"26136","(26136) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Muawiyah said: There is no dream except experiences."
"26137","(26137) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wahram, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Knowledge was not created, or what was carried. Knowledge is like the veil of a dream."
"26138","(26138) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zayd, who said: I heard Burd, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: What was gathered One thing to another is more beautiful than knowledge to dream."
"26139","(26139) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ar’ara bin Al-Barand narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Al-Ahnaf bin Qais said: I am not a dreamer, but I dream."
"26140","(26140) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Do not spread your shame except with those who seek you. (Ahmed 360)"
"26141","(26141) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Do not spread your pride except with whomever you want."
"26142","(26142) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: Do not narrate a hadith except to one who knows it, for whoever does not He knows that it harms him, but does not benefit him."
"26143","(26143) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ammar al-Daniy, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: I will not spread my uniform around. Who does not want it?"
"26144","(26144) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: No. You only distribute your goods to those who want them."
"26145","(26145) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The best of your ankles is ithamed, it sharpens eyesight and makes it grow. Poetry"
"26146","(26146) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: You should wear clothing when sleeping, as it strengthens eyesight and makes hair grow."
"26147","(26147) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Anas, that he used to use kohl three times in each... An eye"
"26148","(26148) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to apply kohl twice in that case, And two in that, and one in between."
"26149","(26149) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, he said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he uses kohl with antimony. He uses kohl to the right three times, and to the left with two times."
"26150","(26150) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had kohl, of which he used three kohls for each eye."
"26151","(26151) Hussein bin Abdul Rahman Al Harithi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al Nadr bin Anas, that he said in Kohl: As for me, I use kohl three times here, three times there, and one in between. I mentioned that to Muhammad, and he said: As for I smear kohl on three here, two here, and one between them."
"26152","(26152) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ma`shar, on the authority of Abu al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: Whoever uses kohl should wear it. (Abu Dawud 36. Ahmad 2/351)"
"26153","(26153) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Sudair, who said: I was with Abu Ja`far, and when I wanted to ride, he took with the passengers and said: You do not have to rent it, and there is no harm in it."
"26154","(26154) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Amir, who said: Omar called Zayd bin Suhan, and they set him on a journey as You host your princes. Then he turned to the people and said: Do the same to Zaid and his companions."
"26155","(26155) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Perhaps Ibn Abbas, or Ibn Omar in the stirrup."
"26156","(26156) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, who said: I saw Ibrahim, a one-eyed boy, taking his hand. With stirrups, I think it is. He said: Friday."
"26157","(26157) Affan told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told us, he said: Abdullah bin Subih al-Hanafi told us, and he said To ride, and a man took his stirrup and said: I heard that a mutarrif used to say: I would not prevent a brother of mine who wants my honour. To honor me."
"26158","(26158) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, he said: Ghalib al-Qattan told us, he said: One day I wanted to ride A donkey, then Shuaib came holding the stirrups, so I asked Al-Hasan and he said: Accept your brother’s dignity."
"26159","(26159) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Yusuf bin Why, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever borrows knowledge from the stars has borrowed his people from Magic, more and more. (Abu Dawud 3900; Ibn Majah 3726)"
"26160","(26160) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in learning from the stars and the moon what he finds his way. With it"
"26161","(26161) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to me, saying: Abdullah bin Tawus narrated to us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: They looked at the stars and at the letters of Abu Jad. He said: I see that these are a people who have no creation."
"26162","(26162) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: Omar said: Learn from this. The stars are what you are guided by in the darkness of land and sea, then they caught you."
"26163","(26163) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to beat He was born to the tune."
"26164","(26164) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Omar bin Zaid, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: As for after So they understood the Sunnah and understood the Arabic."
"26165","(26165) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Suleiman bin David to his son: Whoever wants to anger his enemy should not lift the rod from his sons."
"26166","(26166) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They used to say: Honor your child and do good. His manners"
"26167","(26167) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about grammar, and he said: I do not know of any harm in it if it does not exist. There is transgression in it."
"26168","(26168) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, that it is out of hatred, not praise. God"
"26169","(26169) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was disliked for a man to say no, thank God. But say: Yes, praise be to God."
"26170","(26170) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: It is disliked for a man to say no. Praise be to God, but he says: No, praise be to God."
"26171","(26171) Affan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, that whenever Muhammad trimmed his nails, he would bury them."
"26172","(26172) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, he said: Habib bin Shahid told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah said: I asked permission to visit Muslim bin Yassar, so I sat down, then he gave me permission, so I entered upon him and he said: I have asked for permission. Ali, and I will bury some of my children. He said: And some of his wives had miscarried, so he buried them."
"26173","(26173) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, that he ordered a cupper He is forced to empty his cup of blood for a dog to cancel it."
"26174","(26174) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of a man from Banu Hashim, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, ordered the burial of hair, nails, and blood. (Bukhari 2094, Bazar 2968)"
"26175","(26175) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, that it was If he trimmed his nails, he buried them, or ordered them to be buried."
"26176","(26176) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of al-Qasim, that he used to bury his hair with manna."
"26177","(26177) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mahdi, he said: We entered upon Muhammad ibn Sirin on Friday after the afternoon prayer, so he called With scissors, he trimmed his nails and gathered them together. Mahdi said: Then Hisham informed us that he was ordering her to be buried."
"26178","(26178) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I entered the mosque of Medina and saw Abdullah Ibn Salam, so I greeted and then sat down. He said: O son of my brother, you sat down and we want to stand up."
"26179","(26179) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: A man narrated to me, that a man sat next to Al-Hasan and he said to him: You sat with us on When one of us rises, shall I give the call to prayer?"
"26180","(26180) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If a man sits towards you intentionally, do not get up until You ask for permission?"
"26181","(26181) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abraham, the same."
"26182","(26182) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: No one sat next to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then stood up until he did."
"26183","(26183) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He saw no harm in a man sitting and asking another man to stand up, and not He seeks her permission."
"26184","(26184) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’, who said: I sat with Sa’id bin Jubayr, and when he wanted to get up, he said: Do you give permission? You sat next to me."
"26185","(26185) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ruba’i, who said: A man from Banu Amir narrated to me who asked permission to enter the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was at home, and he said: Shall I enter? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to his servant: Go out to this man and teach him permission and say to him: Say, “Peace be upon you. Come in.” ? So the man heard him and said: Peace be upon you. May I enter? So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him permission and he entered. (Bukhari 1084, Abu Dawud 5134)"
"26186","(26186) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, who heard Aamir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair saying: You told me Rayhanan, that her family sent her to Omar, but she entered upon him without permission, so he informed her and said to her: Come out and greet him. If he responds to you, ask permission."
"26187","(26187) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Wasil bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Sura, on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari, He said: We said, O Messenger of God, this greeting, so what is the appeal? He said: The man speaks with praise, greatness, and praise. And he clears his throat and gives the call to prayer to Ahl al-Bayt. (Ibn Majah 3707)"
"26188","(26188) Yahya bin Muhammad al-Qurashi Abu Zukair told us that he heard Zayd bin Aslam say: My father sent me to Ibn Omar, so I said: Why? He said: Do not say like that, but say: Peace be upon you. When it is said, “And upon you,” then enter."
"26189","(26189) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Naji, on the authority of Ali, who said: I had two entrances to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: an entrance by night, and an entrance by day, so when I came to him, he was He prays and bows his head for me."
"26190","(26190) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I asked permission to enter upon Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla while he was praying in the darkness, so he opened for me."
"26191","(26191) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Zurayah bin Humaidhah, who said: She responded to Abu Bakr, and we were passing by people and greeting them, and they responded to us more than we greeted, so Abu Bakr said: Still People have been victorious over us since this day."
"26192","(26192) Ghandar and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, On the authority of Omar, he said: I was at Abu Bakr’s side and he mentioned the same thing, then he said: The people have favored us with much goodness today."
"26193","(26193) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abi Al-Bakhtari, who said: A man came to Ali, and he said: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful, and may God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. He said: And upon you, so he thought that he had not heard. He said: May peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful, and may God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. He said: And upon you. He said: Don’t you respond to what I say? Why? He said: Didn't you do that?"
"26194","(26194) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari narrated to me, on the authority of Abu He saw that a man entered the mosque while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting on the side of the mosque. He prayed, then he came He greeted him and said: And peace be upon you. (Bukhari 6251, Tirmidhi 2692)"
"26195","(26195) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan said: Abu Dharr came from the Levant and entered the mosque, and Othman was in it. He said: Peace be upon you. He said: Peace be upon you. How are you, Abu Dharr? He said: Fine, how are you, Othman? He said: Fine."
"26196","(26196) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, that a man greeted Salman the Persian and said: Peace be upon him. May God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. Then Salman said: It is sufficient for you, it is sufficient for you. Then he responded to what he said, then he added another, and said. The man asked him: Do you know me, Abu Abdullah? He said: As for my soul, it has known your soul."
"26197","(26197) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to return greetings as It is said to him: Peace be upon you."
"26198","(26198) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jalad ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said: My father advised me, he said: If He greeted you, so do not say: And upon you, say: And upon you, for there are angels with him."
"26199","(26199) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Rahhal, who said: Whenever al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym refuted Peace be upon you means: He intends to respond to what he greeted."
"26200","(24200) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that when Shurayh responded, he said: And upon you."
"26201","(24201) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, that when he greeted him, he said: And peace be upon you. May God have mercy, blessings, and forgiveness."
"26202","(24202) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a man responds, let him say: And upon you - meaning with him. The angels"
"26203","(24203) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, and Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, that when he was refuted, he would say: And upon you. May God have mercy on you."
"26204","(24204) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Whenever Muhammad replied, he would say: And upon you."
"26205","(24205) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: We were sitting at the Gate of Al-Hasan when a man came to him and said: Tell me. My father, on the authority of my grandfather, said: My father sent me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Come to him and greet him. So I went to him and said: My father extends his greetings to you, and he said: And upon you and your father, peace. (Abu Dawud 5189. Ahmad 5/366)"
"26206","(24206) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I said: To him: Your brother’s children will greet you, then the people of the mosque. He said: And upon you and upon them."
"26207","(24207) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdul said to me God: If you meet Omar, or someone like him, then say hello to him. He said: I met him and said it, and he said: On him, or on him. May God’s peace and mercy be upon you."
"26208","(24208) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Aisha She told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Gabriel recites peace be upon you, and she said: And peace be upon him. May God have mercy on you.\n(Bukhari 6253. Tirmidhi 2693)"
"26209","(24209) Muadh bin Muadh and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Whenever Muhammad was told, “So-and-so is reciting to you.” Peace be upon him, he said: And peace be upon you and upon him."
"26210","(24210) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Jalad ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: He advised me My father, he said: If you meet a man, do not say: Peace be upon you, say: Peace be upon you."
"26211","(24211) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Bayan, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, That a man greeted Abu Bakr and said: Peace be upon you, O successor of the Messenger of God. Abu Bakr said: From among these people. All of you"
"26212","(24212) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Al-Salt said: Ibn Sirin came to Ibn Hubaira and said: Peace be upon you, and he said: Ibn Hubaira: What This peace? He said: This is how he used to greet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tirmidhi 2489 and Abu Dawud 5153)"
"26213","(24213) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan said: Abu Dharr came from the Levant and entered the mosque, and Othman was there, and he said: Peace be upon you."
"26214","(24214) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hassan narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Omar came to the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon the Messenger of God, peace be upon you. (Bukhari 1085. Ahmad 1/325)"
"26215","(26215) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: He used to greet Omar. Peace be upon you, Amir. Believers, peace be upon you, meaning upon those who are with you."
"26216","(26216) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to hate even saying peace be upon you. He says peace be upon you."
"26217","(24217) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man greets another man, even if he is alone Let him say, “Peace be upon you,” meaning the angels."
"26218","(24218) Abu Osama, on the authority of Abdul-Mu’min, he said: I greeted a man walking with Muslim bin Yassar, and I said: Peace be upon you, and he said To a Muslim: M, so I said: I recognized him, and he said: And when you greet him, say: Peace be upon you, for he is with him as a guardian."
"26219","(24219) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaffar, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: A man came to Salman and said: So-and-so He greeted you and said: How long has it been? He mentioned a few days and said: If you had not done so, it would have been a trust you would fulfill."
"26220","(24220) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abdul A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah; Concerning a man who says: Convey greetings to so-and-so. They say: This is a wish, unless he forgets it."
"26221","(24221) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I said to Abu Majliz: A man says to another man: Convey greetings to so-and-so, but do not He was embarrassed, he said: This is a trust, and when he said: I will inform you, he was on a quest."
"26222","(24222) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaffar, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hajjimi, on the authority of Abu Jari Al-Hujaimi, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God. He said: Do not say: Upon you. Peace be upon you, for peace be upon you is the life of the dead."
"26223","(24223) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, that a man greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Peace be upon you, O Prophet of God. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked that and said: This is the life of the dead."
"26224","(24224) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, that he disliked saying: Peace be upon you. He said: {And peace be upon the messengers}."
"26225","(24225) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I was walking with Abdullah bin Abi Zakariya was in the land of the Byzantines, and my animal urinated, then it got up and urinated, so I caught up with him, and he said: Have you not greeted? So I said: I have only separated from you now. He said: Even if you separated from me, the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would talk to each other and you would disperse. There will be a tree between them, and they will meet and greet one another."
"26226","(24226) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The two men were among the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They travel together, and the trees separate between them, and they meet, and one greets the other."
"26227","(24227) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Abi al-Bakhtari, and Sa’id ibn Jubayr. Indeed, they were complaining about their bellies, so they would come and greet each other."
"26228","(26228) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim: He would not leave me except with a greeting. I would come and then go. He greets me, then I come, then I go, and he greets me."
"26229","(26229) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, who said: If the man is one of them, he will separate His companion, nothing came between him except a tree, then he met him and greeted him."
"26230","(24230) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: They remembered shaking hands, so Al-Nu’man bin Humaid said: I entered upon Ali. Salman was with my uncle Abbad bin Shurahbil. When he saw him, Salman shook hands with him."
"26231","(24231) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There is no two Muslims who meet and shake hands without being forgiven before they separate.\n(Abu Dawud 5170 and Ibn Majah 3703)"
"26232","(24232) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hanzali Al-Sadusi, on the authority of Anas, who said: We said: O Messenger of God, should we shake hands with each other? Some? He said: Yes. (Tirmidhi 2728. Ahmad 3/198)"
"26233","(24233) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: They were shaking hands with each other. (Bukhari 6243. Tirmidhi 2729)"
"26234","(24234) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bī: Ibn Sirin used to hate it. Shaking hands, he said: Al-Sha’bi said: The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to shake hands, and when one of them came to A journey that hugs its companion."
"26235","(24235) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: I asked Ibn Aoun about shaking hands, and he said: Muhammad did not do it with us, nor did We do it with it, and when a man extended his hand, he did not withhold his hand from anyone."
"26236","(24236) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, who said: A complete greeting is the handshake."
"26237","(24237) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: One of the perfect greetings is the handshake."
"26238","(24238) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ayyub, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Zuhr, on the authority of Ali ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Your perfect greeting is the handshake. (Tirmidhi 2731)"
"26239","(24239) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Asqalani, who said: Someone who saw Ibn Muhairiz shakes hands with a Christian in a Damascus mosque."
"26240","(24240) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to hate shaking hands with a Muslim. The Jew and the Christian."
"26241","(24241) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The polytheists are unclean, so do not shake hands with them. Shake hands with them, let him perform ablution."
"26242","(24242) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I asked him about shaking hands with the Magians. What did he think? That"
"26243","(24243) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met Ja’far. Ibn Abi Talib, so he adhered to him and kissed what was between his eyes. (Abu Dawud 5178, Hakim 624)"
"26244","(24244) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Dinar, on the authority of Utba ibn Abi Uthman, that Omar embraced Hudhayf."
"26245","(24245) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Balaj, who said: I saw Amr ibn Maymun and Al-Aswad ibn Hilal meet and each embraced Islam. Of his companion."
"26246","(24246) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abbad, who said: I saw Abu Majliz and Khalid, the most righteous, meeting each other. So each of them embraced his friend."
"26247","(24247) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, who said: I saw Abu Nadhrah kissing Al-Hasan’s cheek."
"26248","(24248) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Muadh Al-Adawiyah, she said: It was When the companions of Salat ibn Ashim entered upon him, they would adhere to one another."
"26249","(24249) Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Al-Muhajir bin Qunfud, He greeted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was urinating, and he did not respond to him until he had finished.\n(Abu Dawud 18. Ibn Majah 350)"
"26250","(24250) Umar bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: A man passed by The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was urinating, so he greeted him but did not respond to him. (Muslim 115. Tirmidhi 90)"
"26251","(24251) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Alani, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: Our Prophet commanded us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Majah 3693. Tabarani 7524)"
"26252","(24252) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For a Muslim to greet another Muslim when he meets him."
"26253","(24253) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Worship the Most Gracious, and spread peace. (Bukhari 981, Ibn Majah 3694)"
"26254","(24254) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, he said: Abdullah bin Salam told me, he said: When he presented The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived in Medina. The people fled before him, and it was said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and I came. among the people to look, and when I recognized his face, I knew that his face was not that of a liar, so that was the first thing I heard. He speaks of it when he says: O people, spread your greetings."
"26255","(24255) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’athi Al-Muharbiy, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Suwayd, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to spread the greeting."
"26256","(24256) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another.” Shall I not tell you something that if you did it, you would love one another? Spread the peace. (Muslim 93. Tirmidhi 2688)"
"26257","(24257) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, in Paradise there are rooms whose backs can be seen from their bellies, and whose bellies can be seen from their backs, so he stood up. A Bedouin, so he said: To whom is this, O Messenger of God? He said: He is the one who speaks kindly, gives food, spreads greetings, and prays at night while the people are asleep. (Tirmidhi 123, Abu Ali 434)"
"26258","(24258) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Yaish bin Al-Walid, on the authority of a servant of Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Zubair, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Shall I not inform you of something? If you did that, would you love one another? Spread peace among yourselves. (Ahmad 164, Bayhaqi 232)"
"26259","(24259) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Peace is one of the names. God, so reveal it."
"26260","(26260) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If I were to go out to... The market and I have no need except to greet him and he will greet me."
"26261","(26261) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The most stingy of people is the one who is stingy with peace."
"26262","(26262) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ammar al-Dhani, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that He wrote to a man from the People of the Book: Peace be upon you."
"26263","(26263) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When you write to the Jew and the Christian regarding the pilgrimage So he began to greet him, and Mujahid said: Greetings be written upon whoever follows guidance."
"26264","(26244) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, he said: Muhammad bin Umar ibn Abdul Aziz mentioned the matter of starting the people of Dhimmu with salutations, and he said: You will respond to them, and do not begin them, so I said: So how do you say? He said: I don’t see any harm in starting with them. I said: Why? He said: Because God says, “Then pardon them and say, ‘Peace, for they will know.’”"
"26265","(26245) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad Al-Alani and Sharhabeel bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Umamah, He would not pass by a Muslim, a Jew, or a Christian without greeting him."
"26266","(26246) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, that Abdullah, Abu Darda’ and Fadalah bin Ubaid were They begin to greet the polytheists with their greetings."
"26267","(26267) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Issa, who said: Abdullah said: Indeed, from the head of Humility is to begin by greeting whomever you meet."
"26268","(26268) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, he said: Abu Burda wrote To a man from among the people of Dhimma who greeted him, and it was said to him: Why did I say to him? He said: He began to greet me with his greetings."
"26269","(26269) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Atiyya, and he was a writer. By Abdullah bin Mutarrif bin Al-Shakheer, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Mutarrif bin Al-Shakheer say: There is no man on the face of the earth who will start another. With peace, unless that is a charity for him until the Day of Resurrection."
"26270","(24270) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: If a man passes by a people So he greeted them and they responded to him. He had a degree of superiority over them because he mentioned his greeting to them."
"26271","(24271) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Asim, who said: Abdullah said: The initiator With peace, he raises his companion with reward."
"26272","(24272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Two men have never met except that it was The first is in God, who begins with peace."
"26273","(24273) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Some Jews greeted him and said: May peace be upon you, Abul-Qasim. Then he said: May peace be upon you. (Muslim 11. Ahmad 229)"
"26274","(24274) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If someone from the People of the Book greets you, say: And upon you. (Muslim 1705. Abu Dawud 5165)"
"26275","(24275) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdullah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Janni, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am riding tomorrow to Jews, do not begin by greeting them, for when they greet you, say: And upon you. (Ibn Majah 3699. Ahmad 4/144)"
"26276","(24276) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: When the Jews meet you and say: May peace be upon you, then say to them: May peace be upon you."
"26277","(24277) Abu Usama and Waki` told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Hamid bin Zadawa, on the authority of Anas, who said: We forbade, Or We are commanded not to add anything to the People of the Book over me and against you. (Ahmad 3/113)"
"26278","(24278) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad ibn Abd Allah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Abu Busra Al-Ghafari, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We are going to the Jews, but there is no You begin by greeting them, and if they greet, say: And upon you. (Musnad 668)"
"26279","(24279) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever greets Upon you are among God’s creation, so respond to them, even if he is a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian."
"26280","(24280) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ma’an, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If a man from the People of the Book greets you, say “And upon you.”"
"26281","(24281) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: When he greets you Jew or Christian, so say: And upon you."
"26282","(24282) Yahya bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Zamia, on the authority of Salamah bin Wahram, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Whenever he greeted him, The Jew and the Christian, he said: May peace be upon you."
"26283","(24283) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: If you say, May God bless you, say: With peace."
"26284","(24284) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Majeed, he said: Al-Hasan used to hate it for a man to say, “May God bless you.” To say: With peace."
"26285","(24285) Hussein bin Ali, Anab Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Suqi, he said: Maymoon bin Mihran came to us and said: There was a man who greeted you, and he said: Do not say like that, this is the greeting of youth, but say: May God grant you peace."
"26286","(26286) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like it when a man said to another man, “Long live you.” May God say: With peace."
"26287","(24287) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Alqamiya bin Marthad narrated to me, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah. He disliked it, or he said: He disliked greeting with the hand, but he did not see any problem with the head."
"26288","(24288) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us while we were Two boys, so he greeted us. (Bukhari 6247 and Abu Dawud 5161)"
"26289","(24289) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Hajr al-Qaisi, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by us. May God bless him and grant him peace, and we were boys. He said: Peace be upon you, boys. (Ahmad 3/183, Daraqutni 627)"
"26290","(24290) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shuraih, that he used to greet the boys."
"26291","(24291) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Shuraih used to pass by the boys and greet them."
"26292","(26292) Waki’ and Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash bin Al-Harith, who said: Amr bin Maimun used to pass by us when we were young. Then he greets us."
"26293","(24293) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayy bin Abdullah, who said: Abraham used to pass by us when we were young and greet him. On us"
"26294","(24294) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to greet the boys, but he did not He hears them."
"26295","(24295) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, who heard him a month ago say: Asma Bint told him Yazid said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by us with some women and greeted us. (Tirmidhi 2697 and Abu Dawud 5162)"
"26296","(24296) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Tariq al-Taymi, on the authority of Jarir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. He passed by his wives and greeted them. (Ahmad 3/363, Abu Ali 7506)"
"26297","(24297) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, that Ibn Umar passed by a woman in his shade and greeted her."
"26298","(24298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Bishr ibn Harb, who said: I saw Ibn Umar passing by a woman and he greeted her."
"26299","(24299) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, that Omar passed by some women and greeted them."
"26300","(24300) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zurzur, who said: I asked Ata’ about greeting women, and he said: If they are young, then no."
"26301","(24301) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: Should I greet a woman? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"26302","(24302) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not think that a man should greet a woman unless He enters her house and greets her."
"26303","(24303) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Qurayr, who said: A man came to al-Hasan and said: Greet Ali. Women? He said: Join your family."
"26304","(24304) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, he said: Amr bin Maymun used to greet On women and boys."
"26305","(24305) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Uthman, who said: I saw Musa ibn Talha passing by some women sitting and greeting them. May God bless you"
"26306","(24306) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about greeting women, but Hammad disliked it upon young men. And the old man, and Al-Hakam said: Shuraih used to greet everyone. I said: The women? He said: On everyone."
"26307","(24307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, he said: Abu Masoud said to Abu Abdullah, or Abu Abdullah said to Abu Masoud: What did you hear the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say about what they claimed? He said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “A wretched is the stature of a man,” they claimed. (Ahmad 5/401, Tahawi 185)"
"26308","(24308) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah, that he disliked it, they claimed."
"26309","(24309) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba and Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Rabbuh, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked it, they claimed, then Sufyan recited {Alleged by those who disbelieved}"
"26310","(24310) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: They claimed that his companions were lying."
"26311","(26311) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: They claimed that his companions lied, so do not be false. For lying is a companion."
"26312","(26312) Omar bin Saad Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, who said: My father said to me: My son, grant me some of the hadith they claimed and I will do it."
"26313","(24313) Ibn Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, he said: He said to me Shurayh: They claimed it was a lie."
"26314","(26314) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Habib, who said: I asked Abu Qalabi and he said: They claimed."
"26315","(26315) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: I heard Al-Hasan say: They claimed, by God."
"26316","(24316) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: I forbid him, on the authority of Nabidh al-Jar, and he said: They claimed that. He said: I said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: They claimed that."
"26317","(26317) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he was asked about something and he said: They claimed."
"26318","(26318) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about the man performing Witr on his camel. He said: They claimed that Ibn Umar He used to string the earth."
"26319","(24319) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ibn Abi Amr, who said: It was said: O Messenger of God, how are you this morning? He said: Better than a people who did not attend a funeral and were not sick again.\n(Tabarani 7329)"
"26320","(24320) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I said: How are you today, O Messenger of God? He said: Better than a man who did not fast in the morning and is no longer sick."
"26321","(24321) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: I asked Aisha: How did you become? She said: By the grace of God."
"26322","(26322) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I passed by Amer Al-Sha’bi while he was sitting in his courtyard, and I said: How are you? He said: Shurayh used to be nervous when he was asked: How are you? He said: With His blessings, and extended his index finger to the sky."
"26323","(24323) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Bakr told me, he said: A man said to Abu Tamimah Al-Hajimi: How are you? He said: Between two blessings: between a hidden sin, and a double that none of these people knows about, and by God, I have not conveyed it, nor I am doing that."
"26324","(26324) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: I heard Abraham greeting him, and he said: And upon you, and it was said to him: How? Are you? He said: By the grace of God."
"26325","(26325) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, that a man said to him: How are you in the morning, Abu Amr? He said: Yes, I said: From whom? He said: From God."
"26326","(26326) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: When Ali was asked when he was sick, “How are you?” He said: Good news, and he recited these verses: {And We will test you with evil and good as a trial}"
"26327","(24327) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: A man met Ikrimah in Medina and said: How are you? He said: I am a human being whose hands are split, and I am such-and-such, and I am such-and-such. He said: And he used to interpret these verses as: {And We will test you. With evil and good, tempt us, and to Us you will be returned."
"26328","(24328) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, that Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami Whenever he was told: How are you? He said: It is fine, we thank God. Ata’ said: I mentioned that to Abu al-Bakhtari, and he said: Did he take it? Three."
"26329","(24329) Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: A man met Muhammad and said: How are you? He said: Human beings, I am hungry and cannot be satisfied, and I am thirsty but I cannot quench it."
"26330","(24330) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated for you to have intercourse. Their heels (Dharmi 524)"
"26331","(24331) Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abdullah bin Amr On the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was never seen reclining or stepping on his heels. Two men\n(Abu Dawud 3764, Ahmad 2/165)"
"26332","(24332) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, that Ammar called for Ali A man said: O God, if he is a liar, extend the world to him and make it a resting place for his heels."
"26333","(24333) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: Omar bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Qurayh Al-Kindi, he said: Salman and my father set off until they came to Salman’s house, and Salman entered the house and said: Peace be upon you, then he gave permission for my father to read."
"26334","(24334) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When you enter upon your family, say: Peace be upon you. Greetings from God, blessed and good."
"26335","(24335) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ghaffari, who said: When you enter upon your family, say: Peace be upon you."
"26336","(24336) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: I entered his house with Abu al-Aaliya and he greeted him while he was not in it. Someone, and he said something that I did not understand."
"26337","(26337) Zayd ibn Harun told us, saying: Ibn Aoun informed us, on the authority of Muhammad, in the Almighty’s saying: {And those who did not “Accomplish the dream of yourselves.” He said: “Our people used to teach us to greet us, and when one of us came he would say: Peace be upon you.” Will so-and-so enter?"
"26338","(24338) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, he said: Maqil told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, he said: Omar bin Abdul When the Mighty One enters a house, he says: In the name of God and praise be to God, and there is no strength except with God and peace be upon the Prophet of God. Oh God, open I have the doors of Your mercy {And admit me into an entrance of truth, and take me out by a exit of truth, and appoint for me from Yourself a power and helper} and grant me I have mercy from You, you are the bestower, O God, protect me from above me from being kidnapped, and from beneath my feet from being swallowed up. And on my right and on my left are the accursed Satan."
"26339","(24339) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Whenever Abdullah entered He went around and spoke, then he raised his voice."
"26340","(24340) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his followers, that a Jew from Aleppo belonged to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He cried and said: Oh God, make him beautiful, so his hair turned black. (Abu Dawud 492)"
"26341","(24341) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in saying to a Jew, “May God guide you.”"
"26342","(26342) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Jew came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Pray to God for me, and he said: May God increase your wealth and your children, make your body healthy, and prolong your life."
"26343","(24343) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If Pharaoh had said to me, May God bless you, I would have said And in you"
"26344","(24344) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I asked him about the man. He asks permission to greet me, but I do not allow him to greet him? He said: I hate that he gives him permission while the people do the same."
"26345","(24345) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: No. Say the call to prayer until you say peace."
"26346","(24346) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If you are invited, This is your permission, so greet it, then enter."
"26347","(24347) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, who said: A man asked permission to enter upon another man. The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was standing at the door and said: Enter, three times, and he was looking at it, but he did not He gave him permission, then he said: Peace be upon you, enter. He said: Enter. Then he said: If you had stayed until the night saying, “Come in,” you would not have given permission. Until you begin with peace."
"26348","(24348) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Salih Al-Qadaadi, he said: My family sent me to Sa’id bin Jubayr with a gift. So I went to the door while he was performing ablution, and I said: Shall I enter? He remained silent for three days. He said: Say: Peace be upon you. He said: I entered and he said: I did not see you following the Sunnah, so I taught you."
"26349","(24349) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked permission from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Who is this? I said: I am, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am. (Bukhari 6250, Muslim 38)"
"26350","(24350) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar asked for permission, it was said to him: Enter in peace. He came back and said: I do not know whether to enter with peace or without peace."
"26351","(24351) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu al-Jarrah, on the authority of a man from the people of Hijaz, who said: Your wife said: Bring Abu Hurairah to me so that I may ask him for a fatwa about some of my affairs. So I went to him, and he came with me. When we reached the door, He said: Enter the house, so I entered and said: This is Abu Hurairah, he came and said: Peace be upon you, enter. So we said: Enter in peace, so he returned. He said: Peace be upon you, enter. So we said: Enter in peace. He said: Say: Enter. He said: Peace be upon you, shall I enter? So we said to him: Enter, and he entered."
"26352","(24352) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If you enter a house where there is no one, say: Peace. On us and on the righteous servants of God."
"26353","(24353) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; About a man entering a house, or into a mosque when there is no one there. He said: He says: Peace be upon us and the servants of God. The righteous"
"26354","(24354) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God."
"26355","(24355) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Mahan, in the Almighty’s saying: {So when you enter houses So greet yourselves with a greeting from God, blessed and pure. He said: It says: Peace be upon us from our Lord."
"26356","(24356) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It says: Peace be upon us, and upon the servants of God. The righteous"
"26357","(24357) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you enter a house, do not There is no one in it, so say in the name of God, praise be to God, peace be upon us, and upon the righteous servants of God."
"26358","(24358) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If there is no one there, say: Peace be upon us. From our Lord"
"26359","(24359) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that a man wrote to Ibn Umar: In the name of God To so-and-so, and he said: Ibn Umar: M, the name of God is His alone."
"26360","(26360) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was disliked for the beginning of the Message to be written in the name of God is the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful to so-and-so, and he sees no harm in writing it at the beginning and the title."
"26361","(26361) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr, he said: I write to so-and-so, and I do not write To so-and-so"
"26362","(26362) Yahya bin Yaman told us[corrupt] On the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ismail bin Salman, on the authority of Dinar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, he said: There is no harm in writing: In the name of God To so-and-so"
"26363","(24363) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, the same."
"26364","(26364) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: If he wrote, he wrote: Peace be upon you, as I praise God, there is no god but Him, and to Him belongs all praise, the people of the Blessed and Most High: {To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. And He is Able to do all things."
"26365","(26365) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, who said: I came to Na’im bin Abi Hind and he came out to me. A scroll, and behold, in it, from Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah and Muadh ibn Jabal to Omar ibn al-Khattab, peace be upon you. Then he wrote: To them, from Omar bin Al-Khattab to Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah and Muadh bin Jabal, peace be upon you both, as for what follows."
"26366","(26366) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zayd, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dharih, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, He said: Aisha wrote to Muawiyah: As for what comes next."
"26367","(26367) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: He who read the letter of Othman, or who It was recited to him: As for what follows."
"26368","(26368) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I read the letters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever his story ended, he said: As for after. (Bukhari 7. Muslim 1393)"
"26369","(26369) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, saying: I heard Amir saying: Ziyad said: The chapter of speech that David was given what follows."
"26370","(24370) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that he wrote in His Messages: As for after. Then he said: It was in the Messages of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. As for after."
"26371","(24371) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, he said: My father sent me to Ibn Omar, and I saw him writing: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. As for what follows."
"26372","(24372) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: I read some of the letters of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he spoke. A matter has passed. He said: As for what follows. (Bukhari 1121)"
"26373","(24373) Omar bin Saad Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abbad, on the authority of Samarra, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon and said: As for what comes next. (Ibn Hibban 2856; Ibn Khuzaymah 1397)"
"26374","(24374) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Ibn Numir told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Aba Hamid Al-Saadi told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon and said: As for what comes after you. (Bukhari 9250, Muslim 1464)"
"26375","(24375) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, spoke and said: As for what follows. (Bukhari 4141, Muslim 2137)"
"26376","(24376) Maymoon Al-Zaafrani told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He made a speech and said: As for what comes next. (Muslim 592. Ahmad 3/310)"
"26377","(24377) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Al-Tufayl bin Sakhbara is Aisha’s breastfeeding brother. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for what comes after you.\n(Ibn Majah 2118, Hakim 3)"
"26378","(24378) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he addressed them and said: As for what follows. (Muslim 1874. Abu Dawud 4934)"
"26379","(24379) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Abu Darda’ wrote To Muslimah bin Mukhlid, who is a prince in Egypt: As for what comes after you."
"26380","(24380) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hubaira, he said: Abu wrote Al-Darda' to Salman: As for what follows? Salman wrote to Abu al-Darda’: What comes next?"
"26381","(24381) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: As for what comes next."
"26382","(24382) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid Allah al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aakim said: Abu Bakr addressed us and said: As for what follows."
"26383","(24383) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Rahman ibn Dalaf, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his uncle His father, Bilal bin Al-Harith, said: He addressed Omar bin Al-Khattab and said: As for what follows."
"26384","(24384) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Abu Musa wrote to Amer bin Abdullah, who He was called Ibn Abd al-Qais: As for after you."
"26385","(24385) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: I came with Abdullah from the armed forces. He was accompanied by two men from the people of Al-Hira, and when they entered Kufa, they took a different path than theirs, so he turned to them. He saw that they had acted justly, so he greeted them, and I said: May I greet these infidels? He said: Yes, they have been my companions and my companions. Right"
"26386","(24386) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: “Abd did not increase them.” God is about to give signs."
"26387","(24387) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, who said: I was with Ali bin Abdullah Al-Bariqi. Then a Jew or a Christian passed by us, bringing him a package of food, and he greeted Ali, and Shuaib said: So I said: It is. Whether a Jew or a Christian, he recited to me the last Surah Az-Zukhruf {And it was said to him: O my Lord, these are a people who do not believe, so forgive. About them and say, “Peace,” and they will know."
"26388","(24388) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Muammar narrated to us, he said: It has informed me that Abba A woman passed by a Jew and greeted him. It was said to him: He is a Jew. He said: O Jew, return my greetings to me. And I pray for you. He said: I have rejected him. He said: Oh God, increase his wealth and his children."
"26389","(24389) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The rider greets the one walking, and the one walking greets the one sitting, So when they meet, the best of both will begin."
"26390","(24390) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: It was me and Al-Sha’bi, and we met a man riding, so he started with him. Al-Shaabi greeted me with greetings, so I said: Will you start it while we are two men and he is riding? He said: I saw Sharih greeting the passenger."
"26391","(26391) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul and Suleiman bin Musa, who said: The young greet the old. The one who is standing is greeted by the one sitting, the one who is riding is greeted by the one who is walking, and the few are greeted by the many."
"26392","(24392) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Al-Zanba’, on the authority of Abu Al-Dhaqani, who said: It was said to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: Here is a boy from the people of Hira. I have never seen anyone better memorized than him, nor more able to write than him. I thought that you should take him as a scribe in your hands, if you had the need to be your witness. He said: Then Omar said: Then you have taken him as an entourage. Other than the believers."
"26393","(26393) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah had a Christian scribe."
"26394","(24394) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Iyad al-Ash’ari, that Abu Musa had a scribe. Christian"
"26395","(24395) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: The letter of Abu Bakr came to us while we were in Al-Qadisiyah. Abdullah bin Al-Arqam wrote:"
"26396","(24396) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, that Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’ was Ali’s scribe. He told him"
"26397","(24397) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Zaid bin It is established that Abu Bakr said to him: You were writing the revelation to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so compile the Qur’an. So write it down.\n(Bukhari 4679. Tirmidhi 3103)"
"26398","(24398) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali’s writer."
"26399","(24399) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: Ward, the writer of Al-Mughirah bin His people"
"26400","(26400) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Bajaliya, who said: I was the clerk of Jazi bin Muawiyah."
"26401","(24401) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Atiyya, a writer for Abdullah Ibn Mutarrif."
"26402","(26402) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Shu’abi informed us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Hadrami wrote to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he started with himself. (Abu Dawud 5092, Hakim 636)"
"26403","(24403) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Abu Musa wrote: From Abdullah bin Qays to Amer. Bin Abdullah"
"26404","(24404) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, that Ibn Umar wrote to Umar bin Al-Khattab wrote: From Abdullah bin Omar to Omar. Ja’far said: Maymun said: It is only something by which foreigners venerate one another. Some"
"26405","(26405) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of a whisper, he said: Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar said to me: Or will there be embarrassment for me? Should I not begin with him in the Book, for it only begins with a trustworthy man, and a man begins with his father."
"26406","(26406) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: I wrote to my people in Baghdad, beginning with his name, so he wrote to me to forbid me. It is mentioned that the ruling was disliked by him."
"26407","(26407) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of a sheikh, that Zayd bin Thabit wrote to Mu’awiyah, and he began With your help"
"26408","(26408) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to write to him. So he started with it, but did not see any harm in it."
"26409","(26409) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar had a need for Muawiyah. So he wanted to write to him, so they said: If I had started with it. They did not stop talking about it until he wrote: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Muawiyah"
"26410","(26410) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: A man wrote a letter from Al-Hasan to Salih bin Abdul-Rahman, and he wrote: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, from good to good. Then the man said: O Abu Sa’id, if you started with him, so he started with him."
"26411","(26411) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Makki, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Nakha’i that they did not see any harm in A man writes to another man and he begins with him."
"26412","(26412) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: It is okay to start. With someone else if you write to him."
"26413","(24413) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Maimunah, who said: I heard Abu Rafi’ narrate, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Zainab’s name was Bara, so it was said to her: She should purify herself, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named her. May peace and blessings be upon Zainab.\n(Muslim 17 Ahmad 2/430)"
"26414","(26414) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Omar’s son was called Asiya, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called her Jamila (Muslim 15. Abu Dawud 4913)"
"26415","(26415) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Khaythami, he said: My father’s name was The ignorant one was dear, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named him Abd al-Rahman. (Ahmad 4/1788 Ibn Hibban 5828)"
"26416","(26416) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the name He turned the ugly thing into something better than it. (Tirmidhi 2839)"
"26417","(26417) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Masoudi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Juwayriyah’s name was Barra, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed her name.\n(Ahmad 1/316)"
"26418","(26418) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that a man whose name was Al-Hubab, so the Messenger of God named him May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abdullah, and he said: Al-Hubab is a devil, and it was the name of a man who was lying down, so he called him the one who was resurrected.\n(Ibn Saad 541)"
"26419","(26419) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: He did not gain Islam from the Quraysh rebels. Not obedient, and his name was disobedient, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him obedient. (Muslim 1400, Ahmad 3/412)"
"26420","(24420) Yahya bin Ali Abu Al-Muhyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umayr, he said: My nephew told me Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his name is not Abdullah. Bin Salam, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, named me Abdullah bin Salam. (Tirmidhi 3256 and Hakim 413)"
"26421","(26421) Zayd bin Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Hani. Ibn Shurayh, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came among his people, and he heard them calling a man Abd al-Hijr, so he said to him: What is your name? He said: Abdul-Hijr, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: You are only the servant of God."
"26422","(24422) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqeel narrated to us, saying: Mujalid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Stolen, he said: I met Omar bin Al-Khattab and he said: Who are you? I said: Masruq bin Al-Ajda’, and Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Al-Ajda’ is a devil. (Abu Dawud 4918, Bazzar 318)"
"26423","(24423) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he hated the servant of his Lord."
"26424","(24424) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qays al-Asadi, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated the servant of his Lord."
"26425","(24425) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: God hates a king."
"26426","(24426) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Samarra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us. May God bless him and grant him peace, that we should give our slave four names: most successful, beneficial, profitable, and easy-going. (Muslim 1685. Abu Dawud 4920)"
"26427","(24427) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I hope, God willing, that my nation will be called Nafi’, the most successful, and the most blessed. Al-A’mash said: I do not know. He mentioned raising it or not, because when a man comes, he says: He has sinned and blessed him, and they say: No. (Bukhari 833, Abu Dawud 4921)"
"26428","(26428) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: You will do worse than that. You name your children after the prophets, then you curse them."
"26429","(26429) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The most beloved of the names to God is Abdullah. And Abdul Rahman."
"26430","(24430) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The most beloved names to him are the names of the prophets."
"26431","(24431) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him: The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abdul-Rahman. (Muslim 1482, Abu Dawud 4910)"
"26432","(24432) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Ibn al-Hanafiy He was nicknamed Abul-Qasim."
"26433","(24433) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Abu Awany told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Ash'ath was the son of Aisha's sister, and his nickname was Abu Al-Qasim."
"26434","(24434) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Mundhir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyah, who said: Ali said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If a boy is born to me after you, will I name him by your name and give him your nickname? He said: Yes. (Abu Dawud 4928)"
"26435","(24435) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: Do not leave fire in your homes while you sleep. (Bukhari 6293, Muslim 1596)"
"26436","(24436) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: A house burned. In Medina on its people, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about them and said: This Fire is only an enemy of yours. So when you sleep, turn it off from you. (Bukhari 6294, Muslim 1596)"
"26437","(24437) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us, so he commanded us to put out our lamps. (Bukhari 6296 and Muslim 1594)"
"26438","(24438) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was disliked for us to leave the lamp on until Good morning"
"26439","(24439) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us on the Day of Al-Hudaybiyyah: Do not light a fire at night. Then he said: Light it and put it out, for it is No people will overtake your advance, nor your hardship. (Nasa’i 8855. Ahmad 3/26)"
"26440","(24440) Amr bin Talha narrated to us, on the authority of Asbat bin Nasr, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you sleep, turn it off. (Bukhari 1222 and Abu Dawud 5205)"
"26441","(24441) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ziyad, on the authority of the mother of a son of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, she said: Abdullah used to order his house to be swept, even if she looked for straw or reeds in it as much as she could. Aliyah"
"26442","(24442) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suriyat Al-Rabi’, she said: Al-Rabi’ used to order the house to be cleaned all One day"
"26443","(24443) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: When Al-Ash’ari introduced Basra, he said To them: What you say is that the Commander of the Faithful has sent me to you to teach you your Sunnah and purify for you your ways."
"26444","(24444) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace: Call by my name, and do not adopt my surname. (Bukhari 3539. Muslim 1684)"
"26445","(24445) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Call upon me by my name, and do not adopt my surname. (Ahmad 313, Abu Ali 1918)"
"26446","(24446) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was In Al-Baqi', then another man called, O Abu Al-Qasim, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned to him and said: I did not help you. O Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Call me by my name, and do not follow my nickname. (Bukhari 2120, Muslim 1682)"
"26447","(24447) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Call upon me by my name, and do not use my surname, for I have been appointed as a divisor by which I swear between you. (Bukhari 6187, Muslim 1683)"
"26448","(24448) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Amra, on the authority of his paternal uncle, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not combine my name with your nickname. (Ahmad 5/364, Ibn Saad 107)"
"26449","(24449) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, who heard Jabir say: A boy from among us was born to a man. He said: So he named him. Al-Qasim, he said: So we said: We do not call him Abu Al-Qasim, nor do we give him favor in kind. Then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned He did that and said: Your son’s name is Abd al-Rahman. (Bukhari 6186 and Muslim 1684)"
"26450","(24450) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: Would he dislike it for a man to call me Abu al-Qasim? And if his name is not Muhammad? He said: Yes."
"26451","(24451) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-Ahwal, who said: We were circling around with a divider, and a peacock started talking to him. And he says, “It,” so we said: Abu al-Qasim, and he said: By God, I have no nickname for her."
"26452","(24452) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with us on some of his travels, and a woman from the Ansar was riding a camel. She became fed up and cursed her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard that and said: Take what is upon her and leave her, for she is cursed. Imran bin Husayn: It is as if I see her wandering in the market and no one offering her anything. (Muslim 2004, Abu Dawud 2554)"
"26453","(24453) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Barzah, While her maid was riding a camel, or a camel, carrying people’s belongings, was between two mountains, and the mountain became too close to her. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to her, and when she saw him, she began to say: May God curse him, may God grant him curse. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who is the companion of the camel? No camel or camel will accompany us. There is a curse on it from God, or as he said.\n(Muslim 2005, Ahmad 4/419)"
"26454","(24454) Shababā narrated to us, he said: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: While the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was walking among some of his companions, a man among them cursed his camel, and he said: Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who cursed his camel? He said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: Delay it on our behalf, and you have responded. (Ahmad 2/428)"
"26455","(24455) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Wathhab, on the authority of Aisha, that it was near. A camel was brought to her to ride, but it turned on her and she cursed it, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not ride it. You are cursed.\n(Ahmad 6/257, Abu Ali 4716)"
"26456","(24456) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: While Omar was walking among his companions and in The people: A man walks a camel of his own from the people and places it wherever he wants. I do not know what he twisted and cursed. Omar said: Who is this cursing person? They said: So-and-so. He said: Leave us behind, you and your camels. Let no cursed camel accompany us."
"26457","(24457) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd ibn Sinan, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Musa, who said: Everything has an honor, and the most honorable He never faced the qiblah in the gatherings, and said: I did not see Sufyan sitting except facing the qiblah."
"26458","(24458) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: When Muhammad slept, he would face the qiblah and sometimes he would lie down."
"26459","(24459) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that Ibn Masoud sat The future of the Qiblah."
"26460","(26460) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The best councils in the future The kiss"
"26461","(24461) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: Everything has a master, and the master of the gatherings is a future one. The kiss"
"26462","(24462) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, who said: No servant has been given better after Islam than May God bless you with a good mind."
"26463","(24463) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Omar said: According to a man is his religion and his chivalry: His character, and its origin: his mind."
"26464","(24464) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abul Safar, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, on the authority of Omar. In the same way"
"26465","(24465) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: {Then if you catch from them guidance} He said: Reason."
"26466","(24466) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Omar said: According to one’s opinion. His religion, his chivalry, his character, and his origin: his mind."
"26467","(24467) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, in the Almighty’s saying: {An oath of a stone} He said: Of the end and the mind."
"26468","(24468) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, in his saying: {a portion of a stone}. He said: a part with a core and a Mind"
"26469","(24469) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabbab, on the authority of Mujahid: {An oath for someone with a stone} He said: for someone with an intellect."
"26470","(24470) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Khalifa bin Husayn, on the authority of Abu Nasr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas {Section With a stone}: with a core."
"26471","(24471) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak {an oath for someone with a stone} who said: for someone with reason."
"26472","(24472) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Shu’ayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade plucking gray hair and said: It is the light of the believer.\n(Tirmidhi 2821 and Ibn Majah 3721)"
"26473","(24473) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Yusuf, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, that a cupper He took some of the mustache of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw gray hair in his beard, so he turned to her, so the Prophet took May God bless him and grant him peace with his hand and said: Whoever grows gray in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. (Tirmidhi 1435. Ibn Saad 433)"
"26474","(24474) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that he used to hate plucking gray hair. (Muslim 104)"
"26475","(24475) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A man was tortured for plucking The gray hair"
"26476","(24476) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hamid al-Araj, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He used to say: Do not pluck gray hair. For it is the light of the Day of Resurrection."
"26477","(24477) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated plucking He was gray haired and saw no harm in his story."
"26478","(24478) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shu’bi, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar say: Al-Qa’ud Between the shadow and the sun is the seat of Satan."
"26479","(24479) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade that The man sits between the shade and the sun. (Bukhari 1174; Abd al-Razzaq 19800)"
"26480","(24480) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of Banu Makhzum, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The letter of the shadow Satan's seat. (Abu Dawud 4788. Ahmad 2/383)"
"26481","(24481) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Nufa’ al-Jamal, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The letter “shadow” is the resting place of Satan."
"26482","(24482) Ali bin Al-Ja’d narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair said: The limit of the shadow and the sun are the seating places of Satan."
"26483","(24483) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, about the one who sits between the shade and the sun: He said: That is a seat. Satan"
"26484","(24484) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Munib, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade sitting between the sun and the shadow. (Ibn Majah 372, Hakim 272)"
"26485","(26485) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: Whoever listens to the conversation of a people while they are He will have haters who will pour perfume into his ears on the Day of Resurrection, meaning bullets. (Bukhari 7042, Abu Dawud 4985)"
"26486","(24486) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Ata’ bin Dinar, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not use the backs of animals as chairs for your conversations, for perhaps someone who rides is better. And I obey God and remember more. (Ahmad 3/440, Darami 2668)"
"26487","(24487) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, that Omar hated Standing on the mount."
"26488","(26488) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Kamil, on the authority of Habib, who said: He hated standing on the mount for a long period of time and being beaten while he was doing good."
"26489","(24489) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, who said: I saw al-Sha’bi and Talha standing at the house of Sa’d bin Talha"
"26490","(26490) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. That Abu Musa asked permission for Omar three times, but he did not give him permission. He said: So he left and Omar sent to him: What is your response? He said: I asked permission to do so as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us three times. If he gave us permission, we could enter, and if not. We will be given permission to return. He said: “You will bring this with clear evidence,” or “I will do it, and I do it.” So he came to the assembly of his people. So he appealed to them, and they bore witness to him, so he left him.\n(Bukhari 2062. Muslim 35)"
"26491","(26491) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Ali said: The first is permission, and the second is a conspiracy, The third is Azmah, either to give the call to prayer or to reject it."
"26492","(24492) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Asking permission is three times: if you are given permission, otherwise go back."
"26493","(24493) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Among the people asking for permission, he said: He said: If a man among them says, “Peace be upon you, let me enter,” that will suffice for them."
"26494","(26494) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: We entered upon Abu Razin while we were outnumbered, so every one of us was He would greet and ask for permission, and he said: When permission is given to the first of you, permission is given to the last of you."
"26495","(24495) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: Two men sneezed at The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sneezed, or named one of them, but did not smell the other. It was said: O Messenger of God, he sneezed on you. Two men smelled one of them and did not smell the other, so he said: This one praised God, and this one did not praise God.\n(Bukhari 6221, Muslim 2292)"
"26496","(26496) Qasim bin Malik Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of Abu Burda, he said: I entered upon my father. Musa was in the house of Bint al-Fadl and she sneezed and he did not smell me, and she sneezed and you smelled her? So I went back to my mother and told her, and when he came to her, she said: My son sneezed near you and you did not smell him, and she sneezed and you smelled him. He said: Your son sneezed and did not thank God, so I did not smell him. This woman sneezed and thanked God, so I smelled her, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: If one of you sneezes and praises God, then smell him, and if he does not thank God, do not praise him. (Bukhari 941. Muslim 2292)"
"26497","(26497) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: It is the right of a Muslim upon another Muslim to gloat at the sneezer if he praises God. \n(Muslim 1704)"
"26498","(26498) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Munin, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We were He was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man sneezed and thanked God, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God have mercy on you. Then another sneezed and I remained silent, but he did not say anything to him, so he said: O Messenger of God, this man sneezed and I said to him: May God have mercy on you, and she sneezed. Why didn't you say anything to me? He said: This man praised God, but you remained silent. (Bukhari 930)"
"26499","(24499) Muhammad ibn Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin did not even gloat at a sneezer. Thank God"
"26500","(24500) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: A man sneezed at Al-Qasim, and Al-Qasim said to him: Say: Praise be to God. When he said, I gloated at him."
"26501","(26501) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that a man sneezed in his presence. So I smelled it, then he sneezed and I smelled it, then he came back the third time and said: You are suffering."
"26502","(26502) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The sneezer smelled what was between you. And between it three times, and if there is more, then it is fragrant."
"26503","(24503) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Ammar, who said: Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa’ narrated to me, that His father told him that a man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: May God have mercy on you, then the second one sneezed and said: He is sick. (Muslim 2292, Abu Dawud 4998)"
"26504","(24504) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Musab bin Abdul Rahman bin Dhu’ayb, who said: He sneezed. A man was with Ibn al-Zubayr and I smelled him, then he sneezed and I smelled him, then he sneezed the third time and I smelled him, then he sneezed on the fourth time and said to him: Ibn Al-Zubayr: You are distressed, so ignore it."
"26505","(24505) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Amr bin Al-Aas said: If one of you sneezes Three times, smell it, but if it increases, do not smell it, for it is a disease coming out of his head."
"26506","(24506) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr, that a man He sneezed in the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I smelled him. Then he sneezed and I smelled him. Then he sneezed and I smelled him. Then he sneezed the fourth time and said to him. : The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: You are in distress, so ignore it."
"26507","(24507) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who sneezes repeatedly, he said: I smelled it once."
"26508","(24508) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said that it is sufficient to gloat over it once."
"26509","(24509) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Munabbih, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who needed to go in to the family of He is protected from rain or hail. Should he seek permission from them? He said: Yes."
"26510","(26510) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Muhammad: How do I seek permission from the People of the Book? He said: If you wish, you can say: Peace be upon whoever follows guidance. Is there a place for you?"
"26511","(26511) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ghaffari, who said: If you enter a house in which The polytheists, say: Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. They think that you have greeted them, and have turned away peace from them."
"26512","(26512) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, that He used to ask permission from the people of the month of memory."
"26513","(26513) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Do not enter upon the People of the Book except With permission"
"26514","(26514) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, that he used to say: Andraim."
"26515","(26515) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Munabbih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man sneezed According to Ibn Omar, he said: Ashhab. Ibn Omar said: Ashhab is the name of a devil, and Satan placed him in the middle of a sneeze, and praise be to God. To be remembered."
"26516","(26516) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to say: Ash’ab, when He sneezed"
"26517","(26517) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he sneezes while alone, let him say: Praise be to God. Lord of the worlds, then he says: May God have mercy on us and you, for it is the smell of whoever hears it among God’s creation."
"26518","(26518) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: If you sneeze and you are alone, respond to someone else. With you, meaning one of the angels."
"26519","(26519) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, and let someone respond to him. May God have mercy on him, and may he reply to them: May God guide you and make peace with you. (Tirmidhi 2741. Ahmad 5/122)"
"26520","(24520) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When he sneezes Let one of you say: Praise be to God, and let those who are with him say: May God have mercy on you, and let him respond to them: May God forgive us and you. \n(Bukhari 934, Hakim 266)"
"26521","(24521) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah used to say that when a man sneezed, he said, “Praise be to God.” They said: May God have mercy on us and you, and he said: May God forgive us and you."
"26522","(24522) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he smelled the sneezer, he said: May God have mercy on us and you, so when he sneezes and you sneeze, he says: May God forgive us and you and have mercy on us and you."
"26523","(24523) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whenever Abdullah sneezed I gloated, and he said: May God forgive us and you."
"26524","(24524) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whenever they smelled a sneezer, they would say: May God forgive us. And to you"
"26525","(24525) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you smell a sneezer So say: May God have mercy on you, and he says: May God guide you and reconcile with you."
"26526","(24526) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Al-Majishun informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he is rejected, let him say: May God guide you and make peace with you.\n(Bukhari 6224. Ahmad 2/353)"
"26527","(24527) Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Yahya And Issa bin Abi Talha and Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talha said: If one of you sneezes, it is said to him: May God have mercy on you, he said: May God guide you and reconcile you."
"26528","(24528) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin narrated to us Al-Harith, on the authority of Marwan ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghouth, on the authority of Ubayy, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: In poetry there is wisdom."
"26529","(24529) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: From poetry Wisdom"
"26530","(24530) Abu Asama told us, he said: Zaydah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he used to say: In poetry there is wisdom."
"26531","(26531) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Hussam bin Al-Masak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, among poetry is wisdom."
"26532","(26532) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, from poetry Definitely"
"26533","(24533) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Ibn Al-Sharid, or Ya’qub bin Asim heard One of them, Al-Shareed, says: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led me behind him and said: Do you have some of the poetry of Umayyah ibn Ubayy? Did you pray anything? I said: Yes, he said:"
"26534","(24534) Talaq bin Ghannam narrated to us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Some of poetry is wisdom, and some of eloquence is magic."
"26535","(24535) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya’la, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of His father, he said: I recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hundred rhymes from the poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt. He says: Between each rhyme:"
"26536","(24536) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utba, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt in some of his poetry, or he said in two verses of His poetry, and he said:\nSaturn and Taurus are under the foot of his right hand, and the eagle is under the other, an observant heir.\n He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He spoke the truth.\nAnd the sun rises every last night, red, and its color turns pink.\n The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has spoken the truth."
"26537","(24537) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He recites from the verses: And he will bring you news from whom you have not provided."
"26538","(24538) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Musa ibn Talha, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: The truest word is said by a poet who spoke to Labid, then acted He took it at the beginning and left it at the end:\n Verily, everything except for God is false.\n Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt almost converted to Islam."
"26539","(24539) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The truest word was said by the poet Kalima Labid: Except every word. Anything except for God is false. Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt almost converted to Islam."
"26540","(24540) Abdo bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, that Hassan bin Thabit sang The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said verses:\nI testified, God willing, that Muhammad\nAnd that Abu Yahya and Yahya are both\nAnd when the brother of Al-Ahqaf rises among them,\nMessenger of Him who is above the heavens from on high\nHe has acceptable deeds in his religion\nHe speaks of the essence of God in them and does justice."
"26541","(24541) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Prophet Hassan asked for permission in the presence of Quraysh. He said: How? What do you do with my lineage among them? He said: I will release you from them as a hair is released from dough."
"26542","(26542) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It was mentioned in the presence of Aisha Hassan, and it was said to her: It is He has helped you and he has done so and so she said: Wait, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God supports you. He improved his poetry with the Holy Spirit."
"26543","(24543) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Hajj The polytheists, for the Holy Spirit is with you."
"26544","(24544) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Hassan ibn Thabit asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, wanted to attack Abu Sufyan. He said: How about my relatives? He said: By the one who honored you, I will make your hair made of dough."
"26545","(24545) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to Hassan bin Thabit: Confront the polytheists, for Gabriel is with you."
"26546","(26546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Khalid Al-Walbiy, who said: We used to sit with the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, they appeal to poetry and mention the matter of the pre-Islamic times."
"26547","(24547) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Osama, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Abdullah bin Rawahih had a neighbor, so he used to keep secrets. His wife cheated on her. He said: One day he had intercourse with her, so he went to his wife and she accused him of having intercourse with her. Ali, but he denied that, and she said to him: Then read the Qur’an, and he said:\nI testified, God willing, that Muhammad\nAnd that Abu Yahya and Yahya are both\nMessenger of Him who is above the heavens from on high\nHe has acceptable deeds in his religion\n She said: I deserve it for you."
"26548","(24548) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: A poet came to ‘Umar and said: I sing to you. So he asked him for help, and he began to ask for it, so he mentioned Muhammad and said: May God forgive Muhammad for being patient. He said: Omar says: He did it, then He greeted Abu Bakr and Omar, and said: God willing."
"26549","(24549) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sulaym, on the authority of Anas, who said: Al-Bara’ represented a line of poetry, so I said: It represents. My brother, with a line of poetry that you don’t know, perhaps it was the last thing I spoke to him. He said: I will not die on my bed, I have been killed by the polytheists. And there are hundreds of hypocrites except a man."
"26550","(26550) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbiy, who said: I was sitting with the Companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Perhaps they will not mention anything except poetry until they disperse."
"26551","(26551) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahhaf, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Abu Bakr was a poet, and Omar was A poet, and Ali was a poet."
"26552","(26552) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, he said: Amir told me, he said: Rabi’i bin Harash told us, A group of people from Ghatafan came to Omar and they mentioned poetry. Omar said: Which of your poets is the most poetic? They said: You know best, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: Then Omar said: Who is he who says:\nI came to you naked and wearing my clothes\nOut of fear, suspicions arise against me\nSo you have fulfilled your trusts and have not betrayed them.\nThus Noah did not betray\nWe said Al-Nabigha, then he said something like that, then he said: Who is it that says:\nI swore and did not leave you any doubt\nAnd there is no school of thought behind God.\nThen he said: Who is it that says:\nExcept for Solomon, when God said to him\nGet up in the wilderness and rebuke it on the way out.\nWe said: The genius. He said: This is the most poetic of your poets."
"26553","(26553) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, that Abu Bakr sought help from those who were suffering from distress. So he encouraged him and said: I have never sought the advice of anyone before you in Islam."
"26554","(24554) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Hassan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, who said: Abu Bakr said: Perhaps the poet said the wise words."
"26555","(26555) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hani, who said: I heard Ali say:\nTighten your belt for death\nAnd do not be afraid of death\nFor death will meet you\nWhen he arrives in Wadika"
"26556","(26556) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Ali bin Abi Talib said to Al-Muradi:\nI want her life and he wants to kill me\nYour virginity from Murad"
"26557","(26557) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of a collector, who said: Ali built a prison and named it Nafi’, then he began He broke it and built a better one, then he said a verse of poetry:\nHave you not seen me well-dressed?\nAfter Nafi', I built a makhis"
"26558","(24558) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, that Omar wrote to al-Mughirah to ask his poets to speak."
"26559","(26559) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I was a prisoner With Ibn Abbas, as we were setting off for Arafat, I used to recite poetry to him, and he would recite poetry to me."
"26560","(26560) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, he said: I went out with Imran bin Husayn. To Kufa, and not a day came upon him without We reciting poetry."
"26561","(26561) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, he said: It was the last A gathering in which we sat with Zaid bin Thabit, a gathering in which we discussed poetry."
"26562","(26562) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We presented Medina, and it, and the environment. So Abu Bakr complained and Bilal complained, she said: Abu Bakr, meaning when he woke up, used to say:\nEvery person brings the morning to his family\nAnd death is closer than the strap of his sandal\nShe said: When Bilal woke up, he would say:\nI wish my hair could stay the night\nAnd did He ever want the waters of a desert?\nIn the valley and around Idhkhar and Jalil\nAnd do they appear to me as Shama and Tufayl?"
"26563","(24563) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She used to imitate these two. The two verses are from Labid’s saying:\nThe gold of those in whose souls He lives.\nThey eat heresy and betrayal\nAnd I remained behind like the skin of a scabby man.\nAnd the one who speaks them will be criticized, even if he does not raise a complaint."
"26564","(26544) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Omar used to imitate this. House:\n To You I turn anxious and distressed \n Objecting to her fetus in her womb.\n Contrary to the religion of the Christians."
"26565","(24545) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Hassan bin Thabit after his sight had faded, and it was said to her: Will you introduce this to you whom God said: {By the one who took care of his pride? Among them will have a great torment. She said: Is he not in a great torment? His sight has been lost. He said: So they recited a verse. He said: To his daughter:\nA sober horse that will not be weighed down by its offspring and will become my foal from the meat of wanderers.\n She said: But you are not like that."
"26566","(26566) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abi Fazara, on the authority of Al-Hakam, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla"
"26567","(26567) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: I have never seen anyone more knowledgeable about poetry, nor It is obligatory, and I do not know more about jurisprudence than Aisha."
"26568","(26568) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: (The contented) is the beggar, then he recited Bayt Shamakh and said:\nA person’s wealth is used for it and he becomes rich. His hypocrisy is more chaste than contentment."
"26569","(26569) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Aamir {And when they were walking around} he said: On the earth, then he recited a verse for his illiterate people:\nHe brought us meat by sea and by sea"
"26570","(24570) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I have never heard Al-Hasan reciting a verse of poetry except this verse:\nHe who dies is not at rest with a dead person, but rather a dead person is the dead of the living.\n Then he said: He spoke the truth, by God. He was alive even though he was dead in heart."
"26571","(26571) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I heard my father saying: I left her, meaning Aisha, before. To die at the age of three, and I have not seen anyone more knowledgeable of the Book of God, nor of its Sunnah, than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Nor with poetry, nor with any obligatory prayer."
"26572","(26572) Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Al-Tayalisi, on the authority of Masma’ ibn Malik al-Yarbu’i, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: Whenever Ibn Abbas was asked about something from the Qur’an, he would recite some of their poems."
"26573","(24573) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, who said: Amir passed two men at the junction of two roads, and they were He backbited him and fell into it, and he said:\nBlessed and well-pleased, free from the disease of intoxication, for Your honor is one of our honors as long as they have become lawful"
"26574","(24574) Yahya bin Wadh narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan Al-Barrad said: When these verses were revealed {And the poets will be followed by the deviants}, Abdullah bin Rawahih and Ka’b bin Malik and Hassan bin Thabit went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while they were crying, and they said: O Messenger of God, God has revealed This verse, and He knows that we are poets, so He said: Recite what comes after it: {Except those who believe and do righteous deeds} you {and prevail} You"
"26575","(26575) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Ikrimah: {And the poets are followed by the deviants} He said: disobedience. The jinn"
"26576","(26576) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far al-Khattimi, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was building the mosque, and Abdullah bin Rawahiha says:\n The most successful is he who treats mosques.\n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says:\n He who treats mosques has succeeded.\n He recites the Qur’an standing and sitting.\n The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says:\n He recites the Qur’an standing and sitting.\n And they are building the mosque."
"26577","(24577) Abu Asama told us, Mujalid told us, on the authority of Amer, that Harith bin Badr al-Taymi was from the people of Basra, he said:\nShall I not inform Hamdan? I will meet her in peace, and no enemy will be safe from her reproach.\nOmar swore, “Indeed, Hamdan fears God, and her fiancé decrees according to the Scripture.”\n And he said:\nThen my head turned gray and our dreams became dulled by the thunders and lightnings of the nightfall around it.\nAnd indeed, our souls will become sweet with death, and we will leave the afterlife as soon as we taste it.\n Amer said: This hadith was narrated to Abdullah bin Jaafar, and he said: We were more deserving of these verses than Hamadan."
"26578","(26578) Zaid told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Qadamah al-Jumahi told us, he said: Omar bin Shuaib, brother, told me. Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: When the people raised their hands from Siffin, Amr bin Al-Aas said:\nThe war broke out and I prepared for it\nThe stress is connected to a stress, then\nJirsha' is the greatest of all\nAl-Harek Branch, Mallawi Al-Thabaj\nThe horses became tired from the strain\nIf he gets wet from the water, he will cleanse himself\nHe said: Abdullah bin Amr said:\nIf I saw a camel standing and watching\nAt Siffin one day, the wolves were young from it.\nIn the morning, the people of Iraq came as if they were\nAnd We brought them cloak as if it were our own rows\nOur millstones turned around and their millstones turned around\nWhen you said, “They turned away quickly,” it would seem to us\nThey said to us, “We see that you pledge allegiance.”\nSpring clouds raised by the sides\nFrom the sea the tide of its waves is mixed together.\nDuring the daylight hours, as long as the stars follow\nbattalions of them, and battalions of them swayed\nAli, so we said, “Rather, we see that you should fight each other.”"
"26579","(24579) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hamza Abi Amara, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz said to Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Allah bin Utbah: What is the matter with poetry? He said: Is the source able to do anything but blow?"
"26580","(26580) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: When I met Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah It is as if I will cause a sea to explode with it."
"26581","(26581) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said: There were no companions of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, they were moved, not dead, and they used to recite poetry in their gatherings, and they mentioned the matter of Their ignorance, so if one of them is tried to practice any part of his religion, his eyes turn as if he were crazy."
"26582","(26582) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, he said: I heard him say that Al-Farazdaq was one of the most poetic people."
"26583","(24583) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Al-Saadi, who said: I heard Al-Hasan reciting this verse:\nThe young man would be pleased with the piety he showed when he knew the pest that killed him."
"26584","(24584) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Aisha, She said: When the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to relay the news, he would recite the verse of Tarfa: “And he will bring you the news from someone who did not You provide"
"26585","(24585) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: I was I would sit with the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my father in the mosque, and they would recite poetry and mention a hadith. The pre-Islamic one"
"26586","(26586) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: A partner informed us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra, who said: We used to go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of us would sit wherever he finished, and they would discuss poetry and hadiths. The ignorant person was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not forbid them, and perhaps he smiled."
"26587","(24587) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: His people informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: I accompanied Imran bin Husayn is on a journey, and there is not a day in which he does not recite poetry."
"26588","(26588) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: A man asked Muhammad while he was in the mosque, and the man He wants to pray: Should someone who recites poetry perform ablution? Is poetry sung in the mosque? He said: And he recited verses from the poetry of that delicate Hassan, then he opened the prayer."
"26589","(24589) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Tomorrow, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Saree’, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, I have praised God with His praise and others have praised you. He said: Come, And start praising God."
"26590","(26590) Affan told us, he said: Daylam bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: I attended a war, and he said: Abdullah bin Rawaha:\nO soul, do I not see you detesting Paradise? I swear to God whether you will come down to me willingly or you will detest it."
"26591","(26591) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Al-Qasim On the authority of Aisha, she said: I imitated this verse, and Abu Bakr said:\nAnd the whiteness of the clouds gives water to the orphans, protection for the widows.\n Abu Bakr said: That is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"26592","(26592) Mu’ammar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not say anything of poetry except He was told nothing but this:\nThis is the carrier, not the carrier of Khaybar. This is the most righteous and pure of our Lord."
"26593","(26593) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the day of Al-Khandaq, and he had a lot of hair on his chest and was shaking with the likeness of Abdullah bin Rawahih, and he said:\nOh God, had it not been for you, we would not have been guided.\nWe did not give alms or pray\nThen they sent down peace upon us.\nAnd keep your feet firm when we meet\nIndeed, the Initiates have transgressed against us\nAnd if they want to tempt us, we refuse."
"26594","(26594) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not turn his back. On the day of Hunayn, he said: Al-Abbas and Abu Sufyan were holding the reins of his mule, and he said:\nI am the Prophet, there is no lie. I am Ibn Abdul Muttalib."
"26595","(26595) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was in a cave and fell down and said:\nAre you but a bloody finger? In the cause of God you have never met."
"26596","(26596) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Humayd informed us, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: :\nIndeed, life is the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajir."
"26597","(26597) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Mu’alla, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that it was He reads (darasat) and says: Darasat is like the taste of soap and talc."
"26598","(26598) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Abi Safiyya, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: Al-Zanim: the mean and clinging one. Then he recited this verse:\nA sin that men treat as an increase, just as the width of the feet has been increased."
"26599","(26599) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Masoud bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Abbad, on the authority of My father, that a man from Banu Layth came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, should I adjure you? He said: No, so he recited it on the fourth day praising him and said: If any of the poets are good, then you have done well."
"26600","(26600) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I did not know what His saying: {Our Lord Open between us and our people with the truth} until I heard the daughter of Dhu Yazan say: Come, I will open with you."
"26601","(24601) Ahmad ibn Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, that Ibn al-Zubayr sought the verses of Khalid while he was circumambulating. At home"
"26602","(26602) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr used to burden them until He takes them out of the gates and says: If my horn were one, it would be enough for me.\nAnd he says:\nIt is not on our heels that our hearts bleed, but on our feet that blood drips."
"26603","(26603) Abu Asama told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, that the people of Syria were fighting Ibn al-Zubayr. And they shout about it: O Ibn Dhat al-Nitaqin. And Ibn al-Zubayr said:\nAnd that is a clear complaint about you, and it is a disgrace.\n Asmaa said: Did they revile you for it? He said: Yes, she said: By God, it is true."
"26604","(26404) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, that Ibn al-Zubayr used to recite poetry while circumambulating the Kaaba."
"26605","(26405) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, that Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab said: The sun will not rise until three people accompany it. One hundred and seventy kings. Did you not hear Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt say:\nShe is not familiar with us among her messengers except that she will be punished, otherwise she will be flogged."
"26606","(26406) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He hated to write in front of poetry, in the name of God, the Most Gracious. The Most Merciful"
"26607","(26607) Hafs, Abu Muawiyah, and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For a man’s stomach to be filled with pus until he sees it, is better for him than for it to be filled with Poetry, except that Hafs did not say: hollow."
"26608","(24408) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus Mawla. Musab bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was shown the lameness. A poet is singing, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take Satan or hold Satan, so that the man’s stomach will be filled. It is better for him to be pus than to be filled with hair. (Bukhari 3588, Muslim 1769)"
"26609","(26609) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: For a man to be filled with pus is better for him than for him to be filled with hair. (Bukhari 6154, Ahmad 2/96)"
"26610","(26610) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’, he said: Abdullah said: Because It is better for a man’s stomach to be filled with pus than to be filled with hair."
"26611","(26611) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uthman, He said: For a man’s stomach to be filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with hair."
"26612","(26612) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Aidh, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Because It is better for a man’s stomach to be filled with pus than to be filled with hair."
"26613","(26613) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amr bin Harith, he said: Omar said: Because It is better for him for a man’s stomach to be filled with pus than for it to be filled with hair."
"26614","(26414) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, that he recited a verse of poetry to Mary, but she remained silent about it. He took him away and said: I hate having a verse of poetry written in my newspaper."
"26615","(26615) Affan told us, he said: Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, he said: Abu Nawfal bin Abi Aqrab told us, he said: I asked Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, listen to poetry in his presence? She said: He hated hadith to him. (Abu Dawud 1477. Ahmad 134)"
"26616","(26616) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to disdain some of the poetry that was lost. The Qur’an."
"26617","(26617) Al-Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, On the authority of Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For one of you to have his stomach filled with pus, it is better for him than To be filled with poetry. (Muslim 1769. Ahmad 1/175)"
"26618","(26618) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi narrated to us, saying: I heard Habib bin Shahid mention, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Quran. Omar ibn al-Khattab said: I am not pleased that I have what I know of the opposites of the word, such as my family and my wealth. Do they not reckon first? I would like to have the same as my family and property. I would like to have the same as my family and property, then the same as my family and property."
"26619","(26619) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Umar said: In the ma’arid there is that which is sufficient, or A man abstains from lying."
"26620","(24420) Uqba bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: Indeed, in the transgressions there is one who abstains from lying. (Ibn Adi 49. Bayqi 199)"
"26621","(26621) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn Abbas that he said: I do not like such and such objections. And so on"
"26622","(26622) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They had words which they used to ward off. Their souls are afraid of lying."
"26623","(26423) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shahid, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman said: : I do not like to have my share of displeasures, such as my family and my wealth. Perhaps you can see that I do not like to have my family like me. And my money, and I wished that I had the same as my family and money."
"26624","(26424) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Do not say to your companion, “You donkey.” A dog, or a pig, and it will be said to you on the Day of Resurrection: Do you think I created a dog, or a donkey, or a pig?"
"26625","(26425) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Moses asked for water for his people and said: Drink, O donkeys. He said: Then God said to him: Do not call My servants donkeys."
"26626","(26426) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to say: When a man says to another man: Oh donkey. O dog, O pig. He will say to him on the Day of Resurrection: Do you think I created him as a dog, or a donkey, or a pig?"
"26627","(24427) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdul Muzani, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abdullah, that Ibn Omar said to a man who spoke to his companion on the day of Friday while the imam was delivering the sermon: As for you, you are a donkey, and as for your companion, he is not. He collected it for him."
"26628","(26428) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Saad, and Abu Bakra, each of them saying: My ears have heard him, and my heart has comprehended him. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever calls upon someone other than his father, and he knows He is different from his father, so heaven is forbidden to him. (Muslim 115, Ibn Majah 2610)"
"26629","(26429) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who narrated it, and said: Who He is called to someone other than his father, and he will not smell the scent of Paradise. When Nu’aym bin Abi Umayyah, who was Muawiyah, saw that, He wanted to claim her, so he said to Muawiyah: I am only an arrow from your quiver, so shoot me wherever you want. (Ibn Majah 2611. Ahmad 171)"
"26630","(24630) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever takes over someone other than his master and does so, may the curse of God, the angels, and the people be upon him. All of you\n(Muslim 1146. Abu Dawud 5073)"
"26631","(24631) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab. On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, on the authority of Amr ibn Kharijah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them while he was His mount, and his mount is interrupted by its water, and its saliva is dripping between my shoulders. He said: Who has called to anything other than His father, or he took charge of someone other than his master, for his action was subject to the curse of God. No declension or justice will be accepted from him, or he said: justice, and no Conjugation"
"26632","(26632) Shababi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, He said: I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. I heard him say: Whoever takes charge of a master without his permission, his action will be cursed. God"
"26633","(24433) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: Abu Bakr said: Infidelity. By God, whoever claims a lineage is not known, and disavows any lineage, even if it is true. (Dharmi 2863, Ahmed 215)"
"26634","(24434) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Sharhabeel bin Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Imamah Al-Bailili saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father and belongs to someone other than his master, then he must do so. May God curse those who follow her until the Day of Resurrection. (Tirmidhi 2120 and Abu Dawud 2862)"
"26635","(26435) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or accepts a friend other than his master, then he must do so. May God, the angels, and all mankind curse him. (Ahmad 1/328, Abu Ali 2540)"
"26636","(24436) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: I came to Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi, and he said to me: What Did he bring you? So I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: For the angels spread their wings for the seeker of knowledge."
"26637","(24437) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shimr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A teacher Everything is forgiven by goodness, even the fish in the sea. (Darimi 343, Abd al-Barr 180)"
"26638","(24438) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antarah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: No man follows you. A path in which he seeks knowledge, except that God will make easy for him a path to Paradise. (Abu Dawud 3438, Darami 345)"
"26639","(24639) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais al-Mala’i, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The virtue of knowledge is better than the virtue of worship, and the foundation of your religion is piety. (Hakim 92. Bazzar 2969)"
"26640","(26440) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf, he said: Omar said: They investigated before To prevail. (Dharmi 250)"
"26641","(26441) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever follows a path seeking knowledge, God will make a path to Paradise easy for him.\n(Muslim 2074. Abu Dawud 3638)"
"26642","(26442) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A man who is not satisfied: a seeker of knowledge. And he seeks the world. (Dharmi 334)"
"26643","(26443) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Learn, for none of you knows. When will he withdraw to her?"
"26644","(26444) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah said: Tomorrow A scholar or a learner, and do not go in between."
"26645","(26445) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salem ibn Abi al-Ja’d, who said: Abu al-Darda’ said: Learn before knowledge is raised, for the scholar and the learner have equal reward."
"26646","(26446) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salem, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: The teacher of knowledge and the one who learns it are alike in reward."
"26647","(26447) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Za``ari, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: A man does not give birth. A scholar, but knowledge comes from learning."
"26648","(26448) Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, the same as him."
"26649","(26449) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of God, he said: The one who follows Hadiths to be told without smelling the scent of the jinn."
"26650","(26450) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Whoever seeks hadith in order to compete with it with the fools, or To impress the scholars with it, or to divert the faces of the people towards it, then he will be in Hell. (Dharmi 374)"
"26651","(26451) Surayj bin Al-Nu’man narrated to us, saying: Falih narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Tuwal Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muammar. On the authority of Sa`id bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever learns knowledge from He seeks the face of God. He does not learn it except to be afflicted with it by a part of this world. He has not found knowledge of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection - It means its smell. (Abu Dawud 3456. Ibn Majah 252)"
"26652","(26452) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I have never known anyone who asked For knowledge on one of the horizons from stolen."
"26653","(24453) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of an unnamed man, that Masruq departed in Harf, and that Abu Sa’id departed in letter"
"26654","(26454) Ali bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Sha’bi narrated to us a hadith, then he said to me: I gave it to you. Without anything, even if the rider is to ride to Medina in what is next to it. (Bukhari 5083. Muslim 241)"
"26655","(26455) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of a man, who said: Al-Sha’bi told me hadiths that we gave you for nothing, And if the rider is to ride on the other side of it, to Medina."
"26656","(26456) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ammarah, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, who said: I came out To Medina, I seek knowledge and honor."
"26657","(24457) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Iyas, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: They spoke Indeed, the hadith provokes the hadith."
"26658","(26458) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Kammis bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, he said: Ali said: Visit one another and discuss the hadith, for if you do not do so, it will be studied."
"26659","(26459) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I heard Ikrimah saying: Remember the hadith, for To revive his remembrance. (Dharmi 619)"
"26660","(26460) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, that he used to come to young writers He presents his hadith to them so that they do not forget it."
"26661","(26461) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Issa bin al-Musayyab narrated to us, saying: I heard Abraham saying: If you hear a hadith, narrate it. When you hear it, even if you speak it to someone who does not desire it, it will be like a book in your chest."
"26662","(26462) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: Reviving the hadith. I mentioned him, and Abdullah bin Shaddad said to him: How many hadiths have you revived in your heart?"
"26663","(26463) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The evil of knowledge is forgetfulness. And wasting it is telling about it to other than its family. (Dharmi 624)"
"26664","(26464) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Umays, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah said: The worst thing about knowledge is forgetfulness."
"26665","(26445) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abu Hind, on the authority of Abu Musa, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed God. And His Messenger.\n(Malik 958. Ahmad 4/394)"
"26666","(26466) Ibn Numayr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Buraydah, On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever plays with dice, it is as if he dipped his hand in flesh. A pig and its blood.\n(Bukhari 1271, Muslim 1770)"
"26667","(26467) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace, so he mentioned something similar to it. (Ahmad 5/352)"
"26668","(264608) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatadah, he said: We have been informed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was asked about playing with the ankles, and he said: It is the facilitation of non-Arabs. He said: His followers hated playing with everything. Something that even hates playing with a stick. (Ahmad 1/446, Bayhaqi 215)"
"26669","(26469) Mu’tamir and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Hassan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Abd God said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade striking with heels."
"26670","(24670) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The parable of one who plays with heels and does not gamble is the parable of one who pays his fat, and does not eat his own flesh."
"26671","(24671) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Because I put My hand in the flesh of a pig is more beloved to me than playing with dice."
"26672","(24472) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Burd bin Muammar bin Yazid, he said: I asked Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the backgammon, she said: May God disgrace the backgammon and disgrace those who play with it."
"26673","(24473) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, he said: Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-Nakha’i narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas says: For a man to be smeared with the blood of a pig until it expands is better for him than playing with heels."
"26674","(26474) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali said: Dice, or chess, is from gambling."
"26675","(24475) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whenever he found dice He broke it in a house and beat whoever played with it."
"26676","(26476) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said Sufyan: On the authority of Abdullah, and Mas’ar fell short of it: Beware of these marked Ka’ab which are severely rebuked, for they are among the The facilitator"
"26677","(26677) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Usama bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, he heard it from him, on the authority of Abu Musa. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed God and His Messenger."
"26678","(26478) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: Whoever plays with the dice for gambling is like one who eats the flesh of a pig, and whoever plays with them other than for gambling is like one who rolls his money. The pig"
"26679","(24679) Waki` told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Bassam, he said: I asked Abu Ja`far about playing with dice, what he thought of it."
"26680","(26480) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Kamil Abu Al-Ala’ narrated to us, saying: I heard the dhaan prayer forty years ago, on the authority of Ali, He said: Because I adorn myself with the essence of destiny is more beloved to me than to adorn myself with a good character, and because I overturn two burning coals is more beloved to me than overturning Kaabin."
"26681","(26481) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Muslim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali When he passed by them while they were playing at dice, their minds would wander until midday."
"26682","(26482) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Marzuq narrated to us, on the authority of Misra al-Nahdi, he said: Ali passed by some people. They were playing chess, and he said: {What are these statues to which you are paying attention}"
"26683","(26483) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he hated playing chess."
"26684","(26484) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of the chess referee, he said: They used to come down The one who looks at it is like the one who looks at the meat of a pig, and the one who turns it over is like the one who turns the meat of a pig."
"26685","(26485) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid, the client of Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, on the authority of Salama bin Al-Akwa’ said that he forbade his sons from playing with fourteen of the most severe prohibitions."
"26686","(26486) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was Ibn Umar. He forbids playing with sparkles."
"26687","(26487) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he passed by a people who were playing with fourteen So he broke it on the head of one of them."
"26688","(26688) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Umm Qutham said: Ali came in while we were playing with fourteen and he said: What is this? So we said: We are a fast that we recite. He said: Shall I not buy you walnuts for a dirham for you to have fun with and call upon them? He said: So he bought us walnuts for a dirham."
"26689","(26489) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Ali bin Al-Hussein used to play games with his family. By the way"
"26690","(26690) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, saying: Nafi’ informed me that Ibn Umar entered upon me. Two of his female slaves were playing with the Shardah, so he hit them with it until it broke."
"26691","(26691) Safwan bin Issa narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ubaid, who said: Salama bin Al-Akwa’ narrated it. His intention is for them to play with the fourteen, and he says: They will lie about it and cause evil."
"26692","(26692) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, that he hated playing games. By the way"
"26693","(26693) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He hated gambling and said: It is a form of gambling even to play. Boys with walnuts and heels."
"26694","(26694) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Najih narrated to us, saying: I saw Ibn Sirin passing by some young men on the day of Eid. They were gambling with walnuts, so he said: O boys, do not gamble, for gambling is gambling."
"26695","(26695) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Everything in which there is danger, so he is one of the The facilitator"
"26696","(26696) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Mujahid, and Tawoos, or two of them, they said: : Everything related to gambling, which is gambling, even children playing with walnuts."
"26697","(24697) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Aslam Al-Muqairi, who said: Whenever Sa’id bin Jubayr passed by the companions of The dice did not greet them."
"26698","(26698) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, that he passed by a people They were playing with dice, so he greeted him without knowing it, then he came back and said: Return my greeting to me."
"26699","(26699) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Ghurab, on the authority of Banana, that Uthman used to rain in the first rain."
"26700","(26700) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mu’ammil, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, that Ibn Abbas was raining, He takes out his clothes until he takes out his lamp at the first rain."
"26701","(26701) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of Yazid ibn Aban, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace It was raining the first rain."
"26702","(26702) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Razin, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ali, that when he saw rain, he would take off his He put on his clothes and sat down, saying: The hadith of a covenant with the throne."
"26703","(26703) Affan narrated to us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas narrated to us, he said: He afflicted us while we There was rain with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and opened his garment to the point of He struck him, so we said: O Messenger of God, why did you do this? He said: Because it is a hadith about a covenant with his Lord.\n(Abu Dawud 5059, Muslim 615)"
"26704","(26704) Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Samimi narrated to us, saying: Hatim bin Abi Saghira narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, that Amr bin Aws told him that his father Aws told him, saying: We are sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he He tells us stories and reminds us. (Ibn Majah 3929. Ahmed 8)"
"26705","(26705) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, who said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami said: Do not sit with any of the storytellers except his father. Al-Ahwas"
"26706","(26706) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: They mentioned, according to al-Sha`bi, sitting with the story-teller as the equivalent of freeing a slave, and he said: Because I would rather free a slave than sit with the storyteller for four months."
"26707","(26707) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: Ibrahim al-Taimimi used to mention in Abu Wael’s house, so Abu Wael flutters like a bird flutters."
"26708","(26708) Jarir told us, he said: Al-Hasan used to tell stories, and Saeed bin Jubayr used to tell stories."
"26709","(26709) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Sabur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to be proud of the people in four things: By our jurist, by our storyteller, by our muezzin, and by our reciter. Our jurist is Ibn Abbas, our muezzin is Abu Mahdhuriya, and our storyteller is Ubaid bin Umair, and our reciter is Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib."
"26710","(26710) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Zayd bin Shajara, that he used to tell stories, His words were consistent with his actions."
"26711","(26711) Ghandar told us, he said: Shuabi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Kurdous, he said: He was a storyteller, He said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Because I sit in... Such a gathering is more beloved to me than freeing four slaves, meaning stories. (Ahmad 3/474)"
"26712","(26712) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw Tamim al-Dari being cut in the The era of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with them."
"26713","(26713) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, saying: I saw Muhammad bin Ka’b. Al-Qurazi narrates."
"26714","(26714) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Why The stories were told at the time of Abu Bakr, not Omar, but the stories were at the time of turmoil."
"26715","(26715) Mu’awiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: A worker wrote to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, saying, “Here are people who are gathering and praying for the Muslims and for the Emir,” so he wrote To Omar: Come and take them with you. So he approached, and Omar said to the doorman: Prepare a whip for me. When they entered Omar, he approached. Their commander struck him with a whip, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, we are not those who, meaning those are people who come from before. The East"
"26716","(26716) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, that Ali saw A man was telling stories, and he said: Did you know the abrogated and the abrogated? He said: No. He said: I was destroyed and I was destroyed."
"26717","(26717) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhudhail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khabab, he said: My father saw me while I was with a storyteller, and when I came back he took the crowbar and said: A horn that has seen the giants."
"26718","(26718) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Ibrahim al-Taymimi, he said: They only made me My sitting here is that I had a vision as if I was dividing basil, so I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: Indeed, basil has an appearance. And its taste is bitter."
"26719","(26719) Shababah bin Siwar told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, he said: Uqba bin Harith told me, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, A man, a storyteller, came and sat in his seat, and Ibn Umar said: Get up from our gathering. He refused to get up, so Ibn Umar sent to his friend. Condition: Stay with the storyteller, so he sent for him and he made him stay."
"26720","(26720) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: It was said to him: Won’t you narrate it to us? He said: I hate to order you to do something that I do not do."
"26721","(26721) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhudhail, on the authority of Khabbab, who said: He saw his son With a storyteller. When he returned, he girded himself and took the whip and said: With the Amalekites, this is a horn that has come up."
"26722","(26722) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A storyteller entered and sat close to Ibn Umar and said to him: Get up. He refused to get up, so he sent for the man who had the police, and he sent a policeman to him, so he got up."
"26723","(26723) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It reached Omar that a man used to tell stories with sight, so he wrote To him: {These are the verses of the clear Book. Indeed, We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur’an, so that you may understand. We narrate to you the best of stories.} Until the end of the verse, he said: Then the man recognized him and left him."
"26724","(26724) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ukil, who said: Ibrahim said: None of those who remember I hoped within myself that he would be spared from him, meaning Ibrahim al-Taymi, and I wished that he would be spared from him, not on him. Oh no"
"26725","(26725) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ - a neighbor of Salama - who said: I said to Aisha or A man said to her: The storyteller came to pray for me. She said: It is better for you to pray for yourself than for the storyteller to pray for you."
"26726","(26726) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: There was no storyteller in the time of the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, nor in the time of Abu Bakr, nor in the time of Omar, nor in the time of Uthman. (Ibn Majah 3754 and Ibn Hibban 6261)"
"26727","(26727) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa’id al-Kala’i narrated to me, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, that Umm Al-Darda’ sent him to Nawfal bin So-and-so and a storyteller with him, who was a storyteller in the mosque. She said: Say to them: So that they fear God and that their admonition to the people be for themselves."
"26728","(26728) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: He was a man who did not cease He narrated, and Ibn Masoud said to him: Distribute your goods to whoever wants them."
"26729","(26729) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ibn Omar said: We kissed the hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 2440, Ahmed 23)"
"26730","(24730) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"26731","(26731) Ibn Idris, Ghandar, and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salama, on the authority of Safwan bin Assal, that some Jews kissed the hand and feet of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Tirmidhi 2733. Ahmad 4/239)"
"26732","(26732) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, that Abu Ubaidah accepted The hand of Omar, Tamim said: And the qibla is Sunnah. (Bayhaqi 101)"
"26733","(26733) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Talha, who said: Khaythami kissed my hand. Malik said: And he kissed My talent"
"26734","(26734) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked for a man to say: Dhiyya."
"26735","(26735) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sa’ad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin al-Hanafiyyah, that he heard a man He says: Oh, he has finished, he has finished."
"26736","(26736) Hafs told us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Musayyab, that he hated everything that has its end: and it is."
"26737","(26737) Ibn Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Musa bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, he said: Luqman said To his son while he was admonishing him: My son, beware of masking yourself, for you will be feared at night, humiliated, or condemned by the Fire."
"26738","(26738) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Khalifa, on the authority of Ubaidah, he said: I saw a peacock on him. Masked like the mask of monks."
"26739","(26739) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, who said: I saw Al-Hasan bin Ali praying, masked. His head (Abdul Razzaq 19840, Bazzar 2886)"
"26740","(26740) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever sleeps with the smell of deep water in his hand and something befalls him, he has no one to blame but himself."
"26741","(26741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Satan attends the fat."
"26742","(26742) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever sleeps with water on his hand and does not wash it and something befalls him should not be blamed. Except himself.\n(Abu Dawud 3848, Tirmidhi 1859)"
"26743","(26743) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, he said: He said: Sasa’a to his nephew: I was more beloved to your father than you, so you are more beloved to me than my son. If you meet a believer, mix with him. And if you meet an immoral person, then get rid of him."
"26744","(26744) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The believer who mixes with people and is patient in the face of their harm is better. Who does not mix with people and does not tolerate their harm? (Tirmidhi 2507. Ahmad 2/43)"
"26745","(26745) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Baa, he said: Abdullah bin Masoud said: Mix with people, visit them, shake hands with them, and practice your religion, but do not speak to them. (Tabarani 9757)"
"26746","(26746) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muslim Al-Batin narrated to me, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father: On the authority of Amr bin Maimun, he said: Ibn Masoud never missed me on Thursday without me coming to him about it. He said: I never heard him say anything. Never, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. Then when it was the evening of, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, He said: So he lowered his head. He said: I looked at him standing with the buttons of his shirt undone, his eyes had sunken and his cheeks had swollen. He said: Or less than that, or above that, or close to that, or similar to that. (Ahmad 1/452, Darami 270)"
"26747","(26747) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Whenever Anas bin Malik narrated on the authority of the Messenger He, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated a hadith and finished it. He said: Or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said.\n(Dharmi 276, Ahmed 205)"
"26748","(26748) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He narrated a hadith, and it was said to him: Should you raise this? He said: Anything other than Him is more beloved to us. If there was an error in that, or an increase, or a decrease, it would be more beloved to us."
"26749","(26749) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: We said to Zayd ibn Arqam. He told us, he said: We grew old and forgot, and the hadith against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is severe. (Ibn Majah 25. Ahmad 370)"
"26750","(26750) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, He said: I went out with Saad bin Malik from Medina to Mecca, and I did not hear him narrate anything until we returned."
"26751","(26751) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: Toubi Al-Anbari told us, he said: Al-Shu’bi said to me: Have you seen? Al-Hasan when he says, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I sat with Ibn Umar, and I did not hear him speak about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, except for a hadith, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought to a lizard and said: It is not one of my food. You, eat it. (Bukhari 7267, Muslim 1543)"
"26752","(26752) Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Shu’abi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I sat To Ibn Umar, a year old, but I did not hear him narrate anything on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Majah 26. Ahmad 2/157)"
"26753","(26753) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said to Ibn Masoud And according to Abu Al-Darda’, Abu Masoud, and Uqba bin Amr: I think this hadith is on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I think he detained them in Medina until he was injured."
"26754","(26754) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Sahl bin Saad say: A man came out of a hole in The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had with him a muddy that he was scratching his head with, and he said: If I had known that you were looking, I would have stabbed him with it. In your eyes: permission is only from sight. (Bukhari 6241, Muslim 1698)"
"26755","(26755) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Barakah ibn Ali al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Suwayd al-Abdi, who said: We were at the door of Ibn Omar, we asked him for permission, then he suddenly turned around and saw me and said: Which of you has looked into my house? He said: I said: May God bless you. I suddenly turned around and looked. He said: Woe to you if you look into my house!"
"26756","(26756) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Al-Hudhayl ibn Shurahbil, that Sa’d He asked permission from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he entered his head, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Permission was only made from... For the sake of looking. (Abu Dawud 5131, Tabarani 5386)"
"26757","(26757) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who came before him? His vision of the houses was destroyed, meaning he entered."
"26758","(26758) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Huzayl, who said: A man came and stood at the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He asked for permission, so he stood at the door, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Such-and-such, and such-and-such about you. For permission is only a matter of waiting."
"26759","(26759) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If someone were to look at people without their permission, it would be permissible for them to gouge out his eyes. (Bukhari 6888 and Muslim 1699)"
"26760","(26760) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Humayd informed us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in his house, when a man came out through the door, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, covered him with a razor. So the man delayed. (Bukhari 6242, Muslim 1699)"
"26761","(26761) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim ibn Nazir, who said: A man asked permission to Hudhayfă put his head in, and Hudhayfă said to him: You have put your head in, so enter your seat."
"26762","(26762) Sharik bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell. (Bukhari 6888 and Tirmidhi 2459)"
"26763","(26763) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies Ali intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell. (Bukhari 1088 Muslim 10)"
"26764","(26744) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, for example Hadith of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib. (Bazzar 621)"
"26765","(26745) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Kabshah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell.\n(Bukhari 3461, Tirmidhi 2469)"
"26766","(26746) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Amir bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his father, He said: I said to Al-Zubayr: Oh my father, why do I not hear you speak on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as I hear Ibn Masoud? And so-and-so and so-and-so? He said: As for me, I have not left him since I converted to Islam, but I heard a word from him: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his place among the people. Fire (Bukhari 1071, Abu Dawud 3643)"
"26767","(26747) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid ibn Salamah, on the authority of Muslim, a client of Khalid ibn Arfatah. Khaled bin Arfatah mentioned Al-Mukhtar and said: He is a liar, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: He who lies Ali intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell. (Ahmad 5/292, Abu Ali 6833)"
"26768","(26768) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Ka’b, on the authority of Abu Qatada, He said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying on this pulpit: Beware of the many hadiths on me, so who said Let him speak the truth, or the truth, and whoever says something about me that I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell. (Ahmad 5/297, Darmi 237)"
"26769","(26769) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Usamah narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Salim, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever lies to me will have a house built for him in Hell.\n(Ahmad 2/22. Tabarani 13154)"
"26770","(26770) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, that he heard Ali making a speech, saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Do not lie to me, for whoever lies to me will enter Hell. (Bukhari 1061 Muslim 123)"
"26771","(26771) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, he said: Zayd bin Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies to me, I think he said: intentionally. Let him take his seat in the Fire. (Muslim 2298. Ahmad 3/44)"
"26772","(26772) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his place in Hell. (Ibn Majah 37)"
"26773","(26773) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Bakr bin Amr narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Uthman Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says something about me? I did not say, “Let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Bukhār 1100, Muslim 10)"
"26774","(26774) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Murā, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose among us and said: You have seen me and heard from me, and you will be asked about him. He lied about me, so let him take his seat in Hell. (Ahmad 5/412)"
"26775","(26775) He said: It was narrated on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his place in Hell. (Ibn Majah 331 Darmi 231)"
"26776","(26776) Zaid told us, he said: Suleiman al-Taymimi told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell, and perhaps he said: Let him take his seat in Hell intentionally.\n(Nasa’i 5914. Ahmad 3/116)"
"26777","(26777) Suwayd bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell.\n(Tirmidhi 2951. Ahmad 1/293)"
"26778","(26778) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu`ba, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A lie to me is not like one of you lying, so whoever lies Ali intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell. (Bukhari 1291, Muslim 15)"
"26779","(26779) Abu Bakr narrated to us, saying: I found in the book of Abu Muhammad bin Abi Shayba: on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Labid, on the authority of Uthman ibn Affan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies to me? Intentionally, let him take his seat in the Fire. (Ahmad 1/701 Bazzar 384)"
"26780","(26780) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Hayyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever lies about me intentionally, let him take his seat in Hell. \n(Ahmad 4/366, Tabarani 5017)"
"26781","(26781) Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Razin, he said: It was said to Al-Abbas: Are you Akbar, or the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: He is older than me and I was born before him.\n(Hakim 320)"
"26782","(26782) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, he said: It was said to Abu Wael: Which of the two of you is greater? Are you Akbar, or Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym? He said: I am older than him in age and he is greater in mind than you."
"26783","(26783) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, in a similar manner."
"26784","(26784) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look into the faces of those who praise The dirt (Muslim 2297, Ahmad 6/5)"
"26785","(26785) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam ibn al-Harith, that a man began to praise Othman, so he went to Al-Miqdad and knelt down. He said: He was a huge man. He said: So he started throwing pebbles in his face. Then Othman said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you see people being praised, dig dirt on their faces. (Muslim 2297, Ahmad 6/5)"
"26786","(26786) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ma’bad al-Janni, on the authority of Mu’awiyah, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Beware of exaggerating, for it is slaughter. (Ahmad 4/98. Tabarani 815)"
"26787","(26787) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymiy, on the authority of his father, who said: We were sitting at Omar bin Al-Khattab, then a man entered and greeted him, then a man from among the people praised him in his face, and Omar said to him: You have been sterilized. May God sanctify the man, may you praise him in his face and in his religion."
"26788","(26788) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ubad Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, Aslam, he said: I heard Omar say: Praise is sacrifice. (Bukhari 336)"
"26789","(26789) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: If one of you asks The pilgrim should make a short request for her, and let a man not come and compliment him on his face and cut his back and say nothing. He prevents him from anything."
"26790","(26790) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, On the authority of his father, he said: A man praised another man in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to him: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him[corrupt] May God bless him and grant him peace: Woe to you, I cut the neck of your companion several times, then he said: If any of you inevitably praises his brother, let him say: To him: I think so, and I do not purify anyone before God. (Muslim 2296. Ibn Majah 3744)"
"26791","(26791) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Asim, who said: I said to Ghanim: Is it disliked for a man to praise his brother when he What a witness? He said: Yes, so I said: Even if he is absent? He said: It used to be said: Do not praise your brother."
"26792","(26792) Abu Dawud Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I will not purify you after the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"26793","(26793) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, That a man was praising another man in the presence of Ibn Omar, so Ibn Omar started pressing the dirt towards his face with his fingers, and he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When you see people praising people, put dust in their mouths? \n(Ahmad 2/94, Ibn Hibban 5770)"
"26794","(26794) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: A man came and praised me. Othman was in his face, so Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad took some dirt and rubbed it in his face, and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: When you meet those who are praised, throw dust on their faces. (Muslim 2297, Abu Dawud 4771)"
"26795","(26795) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, who said: We were He was sitting with Omar, and a man complimented another man in his face when he turned away, and Omar said: You have disgraced the man, may God disgrace you."
"26796","(26796) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: No one will perish after consulting Him."
"26797","(26797) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: Suleiman bin Dawud said: To his son: My son, do not decide on a matter until you conspire with a guide, for if you do that you will not be sad about it."
"26798","(26798) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: God did not command his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. By consultation, except for what he knew of its virtue. Then he recited {and consult them in the matter}"
"26799","(26799) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If people disagree about something, then see how Omar did about it. For he would not do anything unless he asked and consulted."
"26800","(26800) Al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Iyas ibn Daghfal, who said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: A people never consulted without finding guidance. My command"
"26801","(26801) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, he said: Abu Musab Al-Ansari narrated to me, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Ask for your needs with a good face."
"26802","(26802) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Talhah, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Seek Goodness is in good faces. (Ibn Abi Al-Dunya 53)"
"26803","(26803) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Seek kindness with good faces. (Tabarani 983)"
"26804","(26804) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When they gathered together, they hated that a man should go out. The best hadith."
"26805","(26805) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, Umar said: A man who has learned Persian is nothing but wickedness, and Malice, unless his chivalry decreases."
"26806","(26806) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Do not learn the jargon of foreigners, and do not enter their churches. For the wrath descends upon them."
"26807","(26807) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Dawud Ibn Abi Hind, that Muhammad Ibn Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas heard a people They speak Persian, so he said: What is the matter with the Magians after the Hanifis?"
"26808","(26808) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: Abu Al-Aliya spoke to me in Persian."
"26809","(26809) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāṣ ibn Qaym, who said: I heard a sheikh in Mecca say: Ashraf Abu Hurairah was one of the This door is on this market, so he said: O Banu Farukh, you have struck and trampled."
"26810","(26810) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he greeted him, he brought some dates from the charity. Al-Hasan bin Ali ate a date and licked it in it. He said to him: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Bad, bad, it is not permissible for us to give charity."
"26811","(26811) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Mundhir al-Thawri, who said: A man asked Ibn al-Hanafiyy, Concerning cowardice, he said: O my maid, take this dirham and buy it for a yara. So she bought a yara with it, then brought it. It means cowardice."
"26812","(26812) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of al-Zuhri, it was said to him: Did the man protect me before he was born to him? He said: Some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wear their chintz before he was born to them."
"26813","(26813) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: Kinani Abdullah narrated to Abu Shibl, and he was He has no children."
"26814","(26814) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Hilal ibn Abi Hamid, who said: Kananani Urwa Before he was born to me."
"26815","(26815) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of a servant of al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that she said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: O Messenger of God, all of your wives have given you a nickname other than me. He said: You are the mother of Abdullah. (Bukhari 851, Abu Dawud 4931)"
"26816","(26816) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Hamza bin Suhaib, that Omar said to Suhaib: Why do you conceal my father Yahya when you have no son? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called me Abu Yahya. (Ibn Majah 3738. Ahmad 16)"
"26817","(26817) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was We came, and he used to say to a younger brother of mine: O Abu Umair, what did Al-Naghir do?"
"26818","(26818) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in a man covering himself before he is born. No"
"26819","(26819) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, or Jabir, saying: It was in the words of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a recitation, or a sermon. (Abu Dawud 4805)"
"26820","(26820) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The emanation in speech from Shaqaqish. Satan"
"26821","(26821) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Usama, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were comprehensive words that were understood by everyone who heard them. \n(Abu Dawud 4806. Tirmidhi 3639)"
"26822","(26822) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ bin Omar Al-Jumahi informed us, on the authority of Bishr bin Asim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr - Nafi’ said: I think he raised him - He said: God hates the eloquent person among men who penetrates with his tongue. Al-Baqirah with her tongue. (Abu Dawud 4946. Tirmidhi 2853)"
"26823","(26823) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik Ibn Umayr, who said: A man stood up and spoke between The hand of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until his mouth frothed, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Learn, and beware of you. And slanderous speech, for slanderous speech is one of the slanders of Satan."
"26824","(26824) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he hated the afflicted person to listen to Exorcism from calamity."
"26825","(26825) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He used to hate to say Oh God, do not test me except with what is best. And He says: God Almighty said: (And We will test you with evil and good as a test)."
"26826","(26826) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that whenever the messages were gathered with him He ordered it to be burned."
"26827","(26827) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Qays, that Ubaidah recommended that his books be erased."
"26828","(26828) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of Muslim bin Yassar, who said: It was when The book came to him, wiping out whatever remembrance of God was in it, then He threw it away."
"26829","(26829) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, who said: Abdullah was brought With a scroll containing a hadith, he brought water, wiped it out, then washed it, then ordered it to be burned."
"26830","(26830) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I said to Ubaidah: Have I found a book that I should read? He said: No. (Abu Dawud 1480)"
"26831","(26831) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Thalabah Al-Tai, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he hated to The hadith is written in notebooks."
"26832","(26832) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Tha’labiya, on the authority of Abdullah Mu’adhin Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Do not take The hadith has records like the copies of the Qur’an."
"26833","(26833) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he hated karais."
"26834","(26834) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Al-Atik, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, He hated it"
"26835","(26835) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not curse the night, nor the day, nor the sun, nor the moon, nor the wind, for they send a torment. On a people, and have mercy on others. (Abu Ali 2191)"
"26836","(26836) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Thabit Al-Zarqi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hariri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not curse the wind, for it is from the Spirit of God, it brings you mercy. And the torment, but ask God for its goodness, and seek refuge in God from its evil. (Abu Dawud 5056, Ahmed 268)"
"26837","(26837) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of al-Hasan, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was on a journey, and a wind blew, and it uncovered a man’s velvet that was on her, so he cursed her, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: Have you cursed her? He said: O Messenger of God, I uncovered my amaranth, and he said: When you see it, ask God for some of its goodness, and seek refuge in God from its evil. And do not curse her, for she is commanded. (Abu Dawud 4872. Tirmidhi 1978)"
"26838","(26838) Shababā narrated to us, saying: Shu’bā narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Haytham, who said: Asim bin Damra saw a people following a man. He said: It is a trial for the one who is followed, and a humiliation for the one who follows."
"26839","(26839) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: People followed Ibn Masoud and made... They walked behind him and he said: Do you have anything to do? They said: No. He said: Go back, for this is humiliation for the follower and a temptation for the one who is followed."
"26840","(26840) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Antarah, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hanzala, who said: We brought Ubayy bin Ka’b Let us talk with him. When he got up, we stood up and walked with him. Omar followed him and raised the pearl over him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, know what Do you make? He said: You only see a trial for the one who is being followed and a humiliation for the one who follows."
"26841","(26841) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Ibn Sirin did not let anyone walk with him."
"26842","(26842) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Whenever Abu Al-Aaliyah sat next to him, he would stand up more than four times."
"26843","(26843) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, who said : O my sons, learn archery, for it is your best sport."
"26844","(26844) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Salim al-Fazari, who said: Omar passed Ibn Al-Khattab came to us and said: Shoot, for shooting is an enemy and an executioner."
"26845","(26845) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: Sa’id ibn al-Aas said: If I taught my son the Qur’an, performed Hajj with him, and married him. I have fulfilled his rights, and my rights remain upon him."
"26846","(26846) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The angels do not attend any of There is nothing for you other than betting and archery. The best weapons of the believer are the bow and arrow."
"26847","(26847) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by some people who had converted to Islam, throwing stones, and he said: Take me while I am with Ibn al-Adra’. They said: O Messenger of God, We will take and you will be with some of us and not with others. He said: Take and I will be with you, O children of Ishmael. (Bukhari 2899. Ahmad 4/50)"
"26848","(26848) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hadrad Al-Aslami. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by people from Islam who were struggling, and he said: Shoot, O children of Ishmael. Your father was an archer. Shoot while I am with Ibn al-Adra’. Then the people grabbed them by the hand and said: Why do you not shoot? They said: O Messenger of God, shoot me when you said: I am with Ibn al-Adra’, and we know that your party cannot be defeated? He said: Shoot, and I am with you all. (Musnad 629)"
"26849","(26849) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man who converted to Islam. It is said that Ibn al-Adra` said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Huge yourself together, be afraid, separate yourself, and walk barefoot. (Tabarani 84)"
"26850","(26850) Zaid bin Harun told us: Al-Dastawai informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Peace be upon him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Azraq, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Janni, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: God With a single arrow, three people will enter the jinn: the one who made it and expects goodness in his work, the one who shoots it, and the one who supplies it. With it, and he said: Shoot and ride, and if you shoot, I am more beloved to you than that you ride, and everything that a Muslim man entertains with is invalid except Shooting with his bow, training his horse, and playing with his family are from the truth."
"26851","(26851) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Abu Salam al-Dimashqi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Zaid Al-Janni, on the authority of Uqba bin Aamer, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he mentioned something similar to it except He said: And noble. (Abu Dawud 2505. Ahmad 4/146)"
"26852","(26852) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Bilal ibn Sa’d, who said: I caught them scrambling between targets. And they laughed at each other, and when night came they were monks."
"26853","(26853) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Hudhifi getting stronger. Between the two goals."
"26854","(26854) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Adbas, who said: I heard Omar saying: Scare away the vermin. before it frightens you, and be clean, and gather together, and be humble, and make the head two heads, and refrain from semen, and do not pollute In a miraculous abode, and frighten away the snakes before they frighten you, and repair your dwellings."
"26855","(26855) Ziyad ibn al-Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Qalabayah, that when Ibn Abbas left On his way home to the mosque, the neighbors on the road knew that he had passed by smelling good."
"26856","(26856) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, who said: Abdullah used to perfume himself. With perfume containing musk."
"26857","(26857) Ali bin Hafs told us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ubaidullah, a servant of Saad bin Abu Waqqas said: I saw Ibn Umar, Abu Hurairah, Abu Qatada, and Abu Asid al-Sa’idi passing by us while we were in The Book, and from them we find the scent of fragrance, and He is the creation."
"26858","(26858) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to know With the scent of perfume when it comes. (Abdul Razzaq 7934 and Ibn Saad 398)"
"26859","(26859) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadiya, on the authority of Talha ibn Musarrif, who said: Ibn Masoud was known. With the scent of perfume."
"26860","(26860) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mas’udi, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Mina, on the authority of Nafi’, the client of Abdullah, who said: Abdullah was God is one of the people with the best fragrance and the purest white garment."
"26861","(26861) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of al-Shu`bi, who said: Abdullah ibn Ja`far used to crush the musk, then He made it upon his fountain."
"26862","(26862) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab went out on the day of Eid, passed by the women, and found He smelled the scent of a woman’s head and said: Who is this companion of yours? But if she had known, she would have done it and done it. A woman only perfumes herself for her husband, so when she goes out she wears what she wears, or Her servant was overthrown, and the women said that she had gotten up because of an incident."
"26863","(26863) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Amara, on the authority of Ghanim bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Whatever woman She perfumed herself, then came out to produce her scent, so it is a fa’il, and every ‘ayn is a fa’il."
"26864","(26864) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubaid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Any woman who applies perfume and then goes out to the mosque to find a scent will not be accepted. There is no prayer until she has washed herself from impurity. (Abu Dawud 4171. Ahmad 2/246)"
"26865","(26865) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: If one of you goes out to The mosque, so do not touch perfume. (Muslim 328, Ahmad 6/363)"
"26866","(26866) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Bazza, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud said that while he was in Mecca, he smelled the smell of burning coal from his wife, so he swore to her that she would not go out that night."
"26867","(26867) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqi, on the authority of his mother, who said: It was revealed to me. Hamwi, so she touched perfume, then she went out and sent for Hafsa to me: The perfume is only for the bed."
"26868","(26868) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that his wife asked permission to go to her family. So he gave her permission, and he found on her the smell of smoke, so he detained her, and said: If a woman applies perfume and then goes out, her perfume is only a spark in her. Fire"
"26869","(26869) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, who said: Asma visited her sister Aisha, Al-Zubair was absent, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and found a scent of perfume and said: It is not for a woman not to perfume herself. Her husband is absent. (Tabarani 280)"
"26870","(26870) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Faith is sixty, or seventy, or a few of the two in number: The highest is the witness that there is no god but Allah, the lowest is removing harmful things from the path, and the living are part of the faith. (Bukhari 9. Muslim 63)"
"26871","(26871) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Sam’a, on the authority of Abu al-Wazi’, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: I said: O Messenger of God Show me a job that will benefit me. He said: Removing harm from the way of Muslims. (Muslim 2021, Ibn Majah 3681)"
"26872","(26872) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: Bashar bin Abi Saif narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: Whoever visits a sick person, or spends on his family, or removes harm from the path of harm, then He will do good deeds ten times as much."
"26873","(26873) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, who said: A man went out with Muadh, so he said that he did not see any harm on the road except that he turned away from it, so when he saw that man, he made that nothing passed by without that he turned away from it, so he said to him: What? Did he blame you for this? He said: What I saw you doing. He said: You are right, or you have done well. Indeed, he is the one who withheld harm, by means of which a good deed was recorded for him. And whoever has good deeds recorded for him will enter Paradise."
"26874","(26874) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Hilal say: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, who said: The tree of Ali The way of the people, and she was harming them, so a man separated her from the way of the people. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I saw him. He will move in its shadow in Paradise. (Ahmad 154, Abu Ali 3048)"
"26875","(26875) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: There was a branch of a tree on the way that was hurting people, so a man knocked it down and he was admitted into Paradise. (Ibn Majah 3682)"
"26876","(26876) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abi Uyaynah, on the authority of Yahya bin Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It was presented to me You treated my nation with its deeds, good and bad, and you saw in the good deeds of its deeds the evil being removed from the path, and you saw in Her bad deeds are not buried in the mosque. (Muslim 390. Ahmad 5/180)"
"26877","(26877) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail bin Qays told us, he said: I heard Saad say: Fear this cursed one, then he said Ismail: means crowding on the back of the road."
"26878","(26878) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Beware of you. And the cursed ones. They said: What are the cursed ones? He said: It is similar to sitting on the road and under a tree where the rider can take shade.\n(Muslim 226. Abu Dawud 26)"
"26879","(26879) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not descend on a road horse, and do not fulfill its needs."
"26880","(26880) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Khalid ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he mentioned musk and said: It is the best of your perfumes. (Muslim 1766)"
"26881","(26881) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Your best perfume is musk."
"26882","(26882) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Ubaid’s client, who greeted him, on the authority of Salamah, that when He performed ablution, took musk and wiped his face and hands with it."
"26883","(26883) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Abdullah ibn Ja’far used to crush the musk, then He will place it on his mouth."
"26884","(26884) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in musk for the living or the dead."
"26885","(26885) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawad, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Musk is dead body and blood."
"26886","(26886) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked that musk be put in The Qur’an"
"26887","(26887) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked musk for the living and the dead."
"26888","(26888) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran ibn Muslim, on the authority of Ali ibn Amara, who said: Abu Ayyub came, So he wanted to spend the night on a more suitable rooftop for us. He said: I almost spent the night without any obligation on me."
"26889","(26889) Marwan told us, on the authority of Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: I asked Mujahid about a man who sleeps on the roof and not on it. A wall. Mujahid said: This was only said about someone who fell and died."
"26890","(26890) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Amr bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not cut off ties with someone who maintains ties with your father. That will extinguish your light. Indeed, your love is the love of your father. (Muslim 11. Abu Dawud 5100)"
"26891","(26891) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antarah, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah, who said: Abdullah said: Pray to whoever is. Your father continues, for the prayer of the dead person in his grave is to join those who used to continue."
"26892","(26892) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Bilal, on the authority of his father, who said: One of the prayers of a man is his father. To pray to his brothers whom he used to pray. Hammad said: I think so, on the authority of Abu Musa. It was said to Hammad: Bilal bin Abi Are you cold? He said: Yes."
"26893","(26893) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: It is written in the Torah: Love your beloved. And your father’s lover."
"26894","(26894) Zayd bin Harun told us: Abu Aqeel told us: Salma bin Abdullah bin Omar told us that Omar bin Al-Khattab said: Train your newspapers, and they will be more successful."
"26895","(26895) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Baqiyya informed us, saying: Abu Ahmad Al-Dimashqi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr. On the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Cultivate your soil, it will be more successful for it, and the dust is blessed.\n(Tirmidhi 2713 and Ibn Majah 3774)"
"26896","(26896) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Shaybi narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Cultivate your pages for greater blessing."
"26897","(26897) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Dhurayh, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ibn Abbas said: I see the answer to the letter. Ali truly returned the greeting. (Ibn Adi 176)"
"26898","(26898) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I would not have cared if I was the tenth person to ride on a mount after you caught up with us."
"26899","(26899) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, received Two boys from Banu Abdul Muttalib, one of whom he carried in his hands and the other behind him. (Abdul Razzaq 19482)"
"26900","(26900) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Al-Shahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said: Abdullah Ibn Ja’far said Ibn al-Zubayr: Do you remember when we met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, you and I, and Ibn Abbas? He said: Yes, so he carried us and left you. (Muslim 1885. Ahmad 1/203)"
"26901","(26901) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Muwarriq al-Ijli narrated to us, who said: Abd Allah bin Jaafar narrated to me. He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come from a journey, he would meet us. He would say: “So meet me,” or “with good deeds,” or By Al-Hussein, he said: So he carried one of us in his hands, and the other behind him, until we entered Medina. (Abu Dawud 2559. Ahmed 203)"
"26902","(26902) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Attar, who said: I saw Al-Sha’abi standing behind a man, and he said: The owner of the animal has more right to its advance."
"26903","(26903) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, that he hated to ride. Three on a mount."
"26904","(26904) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Whenever three people ride on an animal, one of them Cursed."
"26905","(26905) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Jibril ibn Ahmar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, who said: Abu Radfa Thalith saw me and said: Cursed."
"26906","(26906) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: I went out to Al-Hira to look at the elephant, and I saw Al-Harith, the one-eyed one. Riding, and behind him was a rump. He said: So he said: If three of you had agreed, we would have carried you."
"26907","(26907) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Muhajir bin Qunfud, who said: We were talking to him when Three people passed by on a donkey, and he said to the last of them: Come down, may God curse you. He said: So it was said to them: Will you curse this man? He said: So he said: We have forbidden this: for three people to ride on an animal. (Tabarani 782)"
"26908","(26908) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Zazan, who said: He saw three people on a mule, so he said, “One of you should come down.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the third. (Abu Dawud 299)"
"26909","(26909) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Salman, on the authority of Sayyar Abi Al-Hakam, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, who said: Abdullah was When he prays Fajr, he does not leave any of his family, whether young or old, to knock until the sun rises."
"26910","(26910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Muhajir ibn Shammas, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I used to go out to One of these cowards set a trap for me, so I went out three mornings and saw a man sitting in a place after dawn, I said: Oh Abdullah, who are you? He said: I am Hudhayfy bin Al-Yaman. He said: I said: What do you do here? He said: Look at the sun, where does it rise from?"
"26911","(26911) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, saying: Qays bin Abi Hazim narrated to me, on the authority of Mudarrak bin Awf, who said: I passed by Bilal while he was in Syria sitting in the morning, and I said: What makes you sit, O Abu Abdullah? He said: I am waiting for the sun to rise."
"26912","(26912) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samarra, that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed At dawn, he sat in his prayer until the sun rose."
"26913","(26913) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, who said: It is astonishing for the companions of Abdullah, that they look at the sun from Wherever it rises, do they not know that when dawn comes from a place from which the sun rises?"
"26914","(26914) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Jundub bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, then Al-Qasri said: I asked permission to call Hudhayfy three times, but he did not give me permission, so I returned, and behold, his Messenger joined me and said: What Your response? I said: I thought you were asleep? He said: I would not sleep until I saw where the sun was rising. He said: I told him about it, and he said: More than one of the companions had done it. Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"26915","(26915) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Do not spend the night in a house alone, for Satan is the most passionate."
"26916","(26916) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade that A man travels alone, or spends the night in a house alone. (Abu Dawud 311, Ahmed 91)"
"26917","(26917) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asim bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you knew what is in the lonely place, none of you would have walked at night. (Bukhari 2998 and Tirmidhi 1473)"
"26918","(26918) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid, who said: It was my father. He did not trust his family to have hadith. He and his companions would stay alone in rooms and talk."
"26919","(26919) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Isa bin Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Piety is shirk, piety is shirk, and there is no one of us except us, but God removes it with trust. (Abu Dawud 3905, Ibn Majah 3538)"
"26920","(26920) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Urwah ibn Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked May God bless him and grant him peace about the bird, and he said: It is a good omen, and it should not be rejected as a Muslim, for if one of you sees any of that If he hates it, let him say: O God, no one brings good deeds, nor repel evil deeds except You, and there is no power or strength except in You.\n(Abu Dawud 3914, Bayqa 139)"
"26921","(26921) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No enemy, no bird, no oracle. Then a man got up to him and said: O Messenger of God, the camel has mange. So the camels are tested with it? He said: That is fate. Who has experienced the first? (Bukhari 5717, Muslim 1742)"
"26922","(26922) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: There is no enemy, no bird, no turtle, and no bird. (Ahmed 229)"
"26923","(26923) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Mudarib ibn Hazn, who said: I said to Abu Hurairah: I heard from Your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something, so tell it to him. He said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No enemy, no bird, no Hama, the best bird is the omen, and the evil eye is true. (Bukhari 5740, Ahmad 2/487)"
"26924","(26924) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loves good omen and hates wickedness. (Ibn Majah 3536. Ibn Hibban 6121)"
"26925","(26925) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: His people told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: No enemies, no birds, and I love good omen. (Bukhari 5756. Ibn Majah 3537)"
"26926","(26926) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Birds do not harm except those who purify themselves."
"26927","(26927) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, saying: Al-Furat ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam said: Saad bin Abi Waqqas went out on a journey. He said: The antelopes headed toward him until, when they got close to him, they returned. So he said to him: A man: O prince, come back. So Saad said to him: Tell me from which one you purified yourself? Is it from its horns when it approaches, or from its backs when it turns? Then Saad said at that: Birds for his people are polytheists."
"26928","(26928) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Marzuq Abu Bukair al-Taymi, on the authority of Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas committed With a leper, so I said to him: Are you stuck with a leper? He said: So he went on and said: Perhaps he is better than you and me."
"26929","(26929) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Siba’ ibn Thabit, on the authority of Umm Karaz said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Send the birds to their places. (Abu Dawud 828. Tayalisi 1634)"
"26930","(26930) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his mother, who said: Sa’id’s mother asked Ali’s concubine: Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein used to fly? She said: They were doing well and going on."
"26931","(26931) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Hayyan, on the authority of Qatn bin Qubaisi, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Health, birds, and roads are from the mountain. (Abu Dawud 3902. Ahmad 3/477)"
"26932","(26932) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Haywah, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, who said: Three of Be in it, then he is a hypocrite: he who speculates, or swears an oath, or whose bird returns from a journey."
"26933","(26933) Ali bin Al-Ja’d told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: No deceit, no slander. (Muslim 1745. Ahmad 3/293)"
"26934","(26934) Sharik and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, who said: He was in A delegation from Thaqif, a leper, sent to him the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying, “We have pledged allegiance to you, so return it.”"
"26935","(26935) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr bin Othman, on the authority of Ummah Fatima bint Hussein, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not keep looking at the lepers."
"26936","(26936) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nāṣ ibn Qaym, who said: I heard a sheikh in Mecca narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Flee from a leper as you flee from a lion."
"26937","(26937) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When he greeted a leper, he passed by a leper, and his nose was stuffy, and it was said to him: O Messenger of God, didn’t you say: Neither an enemy nor a bird? He said: Yes."
"26938","(26938) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the sick person is not preferred over the healthy person. (Muslim 1041, Ibn Majah 3541)"
"26939","(26939) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, who said: Ka’b said to Abdullah bin Amr: Do you fly? He said: Yes, he said: So what do you say? He said: I say, O God, there is no bird except Your bird, and there is no good except Your goodness, and we have no Lord other than You. He said: You are the most knowledgeable of the Arabs."
"26940","(26940) Muhammad bin Sawa’i told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, that it was astonishing for him to be pious. The leper."
"26941","(26941) Ghassan bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Why do you not ask us? Are you bankrupt?"
"26942","(26942) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Ibn Abbas said: No man has ever asked me about a question. Unless you know whether he is a jurist or not a jurist."
"26943","(26943) Omar bin Sa’d told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: No one He asks me?"
"26944","(26944) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Urwah said to us: Come to me and receive from me."
"26945","(26945) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Urwa used to talk to people about his hadith."
"26946","(26946) Omar bin Saad told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, who said: I asked Ibn Masoud about things No one asks me about it."
"26947","(26947) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Khaled bin Arara, who said: I came to Al-Rahbi, and behold, I was with a group of people sitting nearby. Of thirty or forty men, so I sat with them, then Ali came out against us, and I did not see him denying any of the people except me. He said: Is there not a man who asks Me and benefits, and those who sit with him benefit?"
"26948","(26948) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: We see it on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab that none of the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says, “They asked me to ask for anything except Ali bin Abi Talib.”"
"26949","(26949) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was greeted with a book he had narrated from some of the books, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have narrated a good book from some of the People of the Book. He said: He became angry and said: O Ibn Al-Khattab, will you be in it? By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have brought it to you white. Pure, do not ask them about anything lest they tell you the truth and you deny it, or falsehood and you believe it. By His hand, if Moses were alive today, he would have no choice but to follow me."
"26950","(26950) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, who said: The Jews were You come to the Muslims and they talk to them and they do well, or he said: they like it, so mention that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and he said: Do not believe them, and do not deny them. Say: {We believe in God and in what has been revealed to us and what has been revealed to you} to The last verse"
"26951","(26951) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas said: You ask the People of the Book about Their Books, while with you is the Book of God, the closest of the Books to a covenant with God that you read, pure and unblemished. (Bukhari 2685)"
"26952","(26952) Ali narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Abd Allah said: No. Ask the People of the Book about anything and you deny the truth, or you believe in falsehood, for they will not guide you and will lead you astray. themselves, and there is not one of them except in his heart something that invites him to his religion, such as wealth."
"26953","(26954) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Saad, who said: I saw Jabir writing with Ibn Sabit on tablets."
"26954","(26954) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmali, who said: I had poor memory, so he gave me permission. Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in the book."
"26955","(26955) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abdullah bin Sufyan, on the authority of his uncle, He heard Omar bin Al-Khattab say: Restrict knowledge to the Book. (Dharmi 497)"
"26956","(26956) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Ammar, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Restrict them. Knowledge of the Book."
"26957","(26957) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Yusuf bin What's wrong, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr who said: I used to write down everything I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And I want to memorize it, but the Quraysh forbade me from that and said: You must write down everything you hear from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke in contentment and anger. He said: Then I stopped and mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He pointed with his hand to it and said: Write. By the One in whose hand is my soul: nothing comes out of it except truth.\n(Darimi 484. Ahmad 2/192)"
"26958","(26958) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’an, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah brought out to me a letter and swore to him. It is his father's handwriting in his own hand."
"26959","(26959) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in writing the parties."
"26960","(26960) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Kibran, who said: I heard Al-Dahhak say, “If you hear something, write it down, even if it is on a wall.”"
"26961","(26961) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, who said: Al-Dahhak dictated to me the rituals of Hajj."
"26962","(26962) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Bashir bin Nayk, who said: I was I write what I hear from Abu Hurairah. When I wanted to separate from him, I brought him my letter and said, “This is what I heard from you?” He said: Yes."
"26963","(26963) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I used to meet his servants and ask him about them."
"26964","(26964) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, that he used to be with Ibn Abbas, so he heard the hadith from him and wrote it down in a traveling messenger, and when he revealed it, he copied it."
"26965","(26965) Suleiman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: I love the book. To oblivion."
"26966","(26966) Suleiman bin Harb told us: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Al-Malih, he said: They criticize The Book is upon Us, and God Almighty has said: {Their knowledge is with my Lord in a Book}"
"26967","(26967) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah, that whenever he heard something He wrote it"
"26968","(26968) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hanash, who said: I saw them at Al-Bara’ writing about Cover them with reeds."
"26969","(26969) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, who said: I heard Ali making a speech saying: I resolve that everyone who had a book should go back and erase it, for people are like that when they follow the hadiths of their scholars and abandon them. The Book of their Lord"
"26970","(26970) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: We said to Abu Sa`id al-Khudri: If only you had written Hadith? He said: We will not write to you. Take from us what we took from our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"26971","(26971) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Aswad Al-Muharbibi, who said: It was Ibn Masoud disliked the book of knowledge."
"26972","(26972) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah. He said: Omar used to write to his workers: Do not write a letter against me."
"26973","(26973) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His servants said to me: Do not write a letter about me."
"26974","(26974) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I wrote a large book on the authority of my father. He said: Bring me your books, so I brought them to him and he washed them."
"26975","(26975) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Children of Israel went astray only because of books. They inherited it from their fathers."
"26976","(26976) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, that Marwan called Zayd ibn Thabit and some people who wrote: He did not know, so they informed him and he said: Do you know that perhaps everything I told you is not as I told you?"
"26977","(26977) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, who said: Abdullah was brought With a scroll containing a hadith, so he called for water and wiped it out, then washed it, then he ordered it to be burned, then he said: I am reminded by God. If a man taught her to someone, he informed me about it. By God, if I had known that it was in the month of Hind, I would have worn her shoes. The People of the Book were destroyed before you until they abandoned the Book of God behind their backs as if they did not know us."
"26978","(26978) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of his father, who said: The entire book I hate it, he said: I think it means the remembrance of God that was in it. I said to Mu`tamir: Does it mean the ring? He said: Yes."
"26979","(26979) Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that he did not write down hadith."
"26980","(26980) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr say: We used to disagree about... Things I wrote down in a book, then I brought them to Ibn Umar and asked him about them in secret. If he had known about them, they would have been the decisive factor. Between me and him."
"26981","(26981) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim. He said: His servants said: Do not immortalize me. A book"
"26982","(26982) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Harun ibn Antar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he was permitted to He wrote and did not hesitate."
"26983","(26983) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Ammar bin Zazan narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Al-Hakam narrated to us, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no man who has memorized knowledge and is asked about it but he conceals it. He will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bound with a bridle of fire. (Abu Dawud 3450. Ibn Hibban 95)"
"26984","(26984) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever conceals knowledge that he has On the Day of Resurrection, God will bridle him with a bridle of fire. (Ahmed 499)"
"26985","(26985) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, saying: He was among those who used to narrate the hadith as he heard: Muhammad bin Sirin, Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and Raja’ bin Hiyawah, and among those who did not follow that were Al-Hasan, Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi, he said. Ibn Aoun: So I said to Muhammad: So-and-so does not follow the tradition of narrating the hadith as he heard it, so he said: If he had followed it, he would have It is better for him."
"26986","(26986) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, that he used to follow the melody in The hadith is such that he conveys it as he heard it."
"26987","(26987) Safwan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Sha’bi that they did not see any harm in presenting the hadith. And he delayed it, and Ibn Sirin used to criticize it as he heard it."
"26988","(26988) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, who said: We wanted something useful in establishing the melody in The hadith is rejected."
"26989","(26989) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, who said: I said to Abu Ad-Duha: The photographers. He said: The photographers."
"26990","(26990) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: I said to him: Do I hear the melody in the hadith? He said: Stand up."
"26991","(26991) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in a man putting it in his hand. The thread reminds a man of something."
"26992","(26992) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated it. To tie the thread to the ring to remind him of the need."
"26993","(26993) Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Mughra’ Al-Abdi, on the authority of Shuraih, that he heard the sound of a drum and said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a tambourine."
"26994","(26994) Yahya bin Saeed and Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: Khaythami said to me: Either I heard Suwaid say: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a tambourine."
"26995","(26995) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah You will meet the maids in the alleys carrying tambourines and smash them in pieces."
"26996","(26996) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (Bukhari) 33561 Muslim 1839)"
"26997","(26997) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Abraham was the first of the people to add The guest, and the first of the people to cut his moustache and trim his nails and become white, and the first of the people to be circumcised, and the first of the people to see gray hair and say: O Lord. What is this? He said: Dignity. He said: My Lord, increase me in dignity. (Malik 4. Ibn Adi 1511)"
"26998","(26998) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Circumcision is a Sunnah for men and an honorable thing for women. (Tabarani 7112, Ahmad 75)"
"26999","(26999) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Five parts of the nature, so he mentioned circumcision."
"27000","(27000) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid and Ibrahim, who said: Circumcision is part of the Sunnah. (Ibn Hibban 354, Bazzar 990)"
"27001","(27001) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Amr ibn Shurahbil, that Abd God said: God loves for His concessions to be accepted just as He loves for His resolve to be fulfilled. (Tabarani 1003)"
"27002","(27002) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah. He said: Indeed, God He likes His concessions to be fulfilled just as He likes His commandments to be fulfilled."
"27003","(27003) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: God loves to His will will be fulfilled just as he would like his resolve to be fulfilled. (Ahmad 1088, Ibn Hibban 2742)"
"27004","(27004) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, who said: I mentioned it to Abd al-Rahman al-Rahhal. He said: Ibn Abbas said: Indeed God loves His attempts to be fulfilled just as He loves His resolve to be fulfilled."
"27005","(27005) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Mundakir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: God loves for His concessions to be accepted just as He loves for His obligation to be fulfilled."
"27006","(27006) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: God likes that His concessions be given as they are. He likes that His will be fulfilled."
"27007","(27007) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: God loves that you give He is pleased with him, just as he likes to be obeyed in his commands."
"27008","(27008) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Nadhar ibn Arabi, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If two matters conflict with you, hold the Muslims accountable. Their families"
"27009","(27009) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not given the choice. May God bless him and grant him peace, between two matters, one of which is easier than the other, unless he takes the one that is easier. (Muslim 1814. Ahmad 31)"
"27010","(27010) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it easy, and do not make it difficult."
"27011","(27011) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet prayed When God sent him and Muadh to Yemen, he said: Make it easy, and do not make it difficult. (Bukhari 3038, Muslim 1359)"
"27012","(27012) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, on the authority of Abu Kinanani, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The nephew of one of the people among them. (Ahmad 3961 Bazzar 1582)"
"27013","(27013) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ibn The people’s sister to themselves. (Bukhari 3528. Muslim 735)"
"27014","(27014) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I said to Muawiyah bin Qurayh: I heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him by Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin: the nephew of the people from among themselves. He said: Yes. (Nasa’i 2393. Ahmad 222)"
"27015","(27015) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaidullah bin Rifa’i, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered a group of Quraysh and said: Is there anyone else among you? They said: No, except the son of our sister, our ally, and our master. So he said: Your sister’s son is among you, your ally is among you, and your master. Of you (Bukhari 75. Ahmad 340)"
"27016","(27016) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Speak on the authority of the Children of Israel, and there is no harm. (Abu Dawud 3454, Ahmed 502)"
"27017","(27017) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: They talked about the Children of Israel, for there were marvels among them."
"27018","(27018) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Abu Kabshah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Narrate on the authority of the Children of Israel, and there is no harm."
"27019","(27019) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Narrate on the authority of the Children of Israel, and there is no problem. (Ahmed 39)"
"27020","(27020) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: May God curse him. Effeminate men, and transvestite women. He said: I said to Ikrimah: What are transvestite women? He said: Women who resemble men. (Bukhari 5885, Abu Dawud 4094)"
"27021","(27021) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jadham bin Abdullah, on the authority of someone who narrated, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the effeminate men who imitate women, and the effeminate women. Those who resemble men. (Abu Dawud 4095, Ahmed 1715)"
"27022","(27022) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, on the authority of Umm Salama, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He entered upon her and heard an effeminate man saying to her brother, Abdullah bin Abi Umayyah: If God grants victory Al-Taif: Tomorrow I will guide you to a woman who will go to the front with four and turn back with eight. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take them out of... Your bio (Muslim 1715. Abu Dawud 4891)"
"27023","(27023) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Al-Eizar, on the authority of Ikrimah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, would not enter a house in which there was an effeminate person."
"27024","(27024) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed Men who imitate women, and women who imitate men."
"27025","(27025) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who raises him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: He will be cursed by the men who cross-dress with women, and he will be cursed by the women who cross-dress with women."
"27026","(27026) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul A’la, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: Women who imitate men are not of us and we are not of them."
"27027","(27027) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, which of the Muslims is better? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.\n(Muslim 650, Ahmad 372)"
"27028","(27028) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: A man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, which Islam is best? He said: That Muslims are safe from your hand. And your tongue (Muslim 64. Ahmad 36391)"
"27029","(27029) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Urwah ibn al-Nazzal narrating on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Shall I not guide you to the possession of all of that? He said: I said: O Messenger of God, your saying: No I will guide you to the possession of all of that. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pointed with his hand to his tongue. He said: I said: Oh. Messenger of God, and indeed we will be taken to account for what we speak. He said: “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Muadh. And whoever knocks people on their noses except The harvests of their tongues. His people said: And the rulers said: Maymun ibn Abi Shabib told me about it, and I have heard it from him ever since. Forty years (Tirmidhi 2416. Ahmad 233)"
"27030","(27030) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Anbas ibn Uqba. Abdullah said: And who There is no god but Him. There is nothing on earth more in need of a lengthy imprisonment than a tongue. (Abu Dawud 159)"
"27031","(27031) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of his father. He said: Omar entered upon my father. Bakr, holding his tongue like this, saying: Behold, He has brought me the resources."
"27032","(27032) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sufyan, on the authority of his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what is the most pious thing? He pointed with his hand to his tongue. (Tirmidhi 2410, Ahmad 384)"
"27033","(27033) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The most deserving thing that has been purified by a Muslim His tongue"
"27034","(27034) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Let none of you say: I am an evil person, but let him say: I am an evil person. (Bukhari 6180)"
"27035","(27035) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Let none of you say: My soul has done evil, but let him say: I have licked myself. (Bukhari 6179. Muslim 16)"
"27036","(27036) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Samak al-Hanafi, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas hate saying: Lazy"
"27037","(27037) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Rashid, that a sister of Ubaid bin Umayr interceded for a man against him. She said: It is only by God and through you. He became angry and said: It is only by God."
"27038","(27038) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mukhtar, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz hate to say: Oh God, grant me charity, but let him say: Oh God, be gracious to me."
"27039","(27039) Zayd ibn Harun told us: Hisham informed us, on the authority of Hafsiya, on the authority of Rabi’ ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: By God, He does not establish a double for a servant on earth until He is settled for him among the people of heaven."
"27040","(27040) Zayd bin Harun told us: Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Iyas bin Muawiyah and I met. In the same race, we mentioned Ibrahim al-Taimiy, and Iyas said: Were it not for his honor upon me, I would have praised him, so I said: Do you know him? He said: Yes, I said: Why did you force the two to do so? He said: It used to be said: The two are part of the reward."
"27041","(27041) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The immigrants said: O Messenger of God, we have never seen anyone like the people we came to. They have bestowed more kindness than many, but have not been better at consoling a little. They have provided us with provisions, and they have shared with us the port. We feared that they would go away with the entire reward, so he said: No, as long as you praised them and prayed to God for them. (Bukhari 217, Abu Dawud 4779)"
"27042","(27042) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath ibn Sawwar informed us, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The hearts have Active and receptive, and verily, it is hers to take care of her and turn her back, so tell the people what they have come to you about."
"27043","(27043) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, who said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us. May God bless him and grant him peace. They were gathering about him, so he went up to the back of a house and spoke to them."
"27044","(27044) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, saying: Abu Al-Umays told us, on the authority of Abu Talha, who said: Anas bin Malik came to Al-Kufa. So we gathered around him, and he said: So we said: Tell us what you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: And he says: O people. They turned away from me, until we took him to the wall of the palace and said: If you knew what I know, you would weep a lot and laugh. For a little while, O people, depart from me, and we depart from him. (Ahmed 180)"
"27045","(27045) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Tell the people what they have come to you with. So when they turn, know that they have needs. (Dharmi 449)"
"27046","(27046) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he greeted us by exhorting us with the greatest fears for us. (Muslim 2172, Ahmad 425)"
"27047","(27047) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, that whenever he saw one of his companions, It means an ease that He reminded them of."
"27048","(27048) Ibn Idris, Ibn Uyaynah, and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Bukair bin Abd Allah ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Adiy ibn al-Khayyar, said: Umar said: Do not hate Allah towards His servants. One of you is an imam, so he prolongs what they are going through, and one of you is a storyteller, so he prolongs what they are going through."
"27049","(27049) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If a man says to his brother: May God reward you with good, then he has conveyed the message in the two. (Tirmidhi 2035)"
"27050","(27050) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaidullah bin Kuraiz, who said: Omar said: If only he had known One of you has the advantage of saying to his brother: May God reward you with good, for you say more of that to one another."
"27051","(27051) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he goes to bed, he says: O God, to You I surrender myself, to You I direct my face, and to You I entrust my affairs. And to You I have turned my back, desiring and fearing You. There is no refuge or refuge from You except in You. I have believed in Your Book which It was revealed, and by your Prophet whom you sent, or by your Messenger whom you sent. (Bukhari 6313 and Tirmidhi 3394)"
"27052","(27052) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: It was When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, he said: O God, in your name I live and die. When he woke up, he said: Praise be to God who He revived us after He had caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. (Bukhari 6312 and Tirmidhi 3417)"
"27053","(27053) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting with Ammar and a man came to him. So he said: Shall I not teach you some words? He said as if he were submitting them to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When you take your bed at night So say: O God, I have surrendered myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and turned my back to You. I believe in your revealed Book and in your sent Prophet. You created my soul. Its life and its death are yours. If you are sufficient for it, So have mercy on her, and if you delay it, guard her with the preservation of faith."
"27054","(27054) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, who said: I heard Amr bin Asim narrating that he heard Abu Huraira, that Abu Bakr said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Tell me something that I will say in the evening and in the evening. In the morning, he said: Say, O God, the Knower of the unseen and the visible, the Creator of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of all things and His King, I bear witness. There is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and from Satan and his partners. Say it in the morning and in the evening and when I took your bed. (Nasa’i 7715. Darami 2689)"
